    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following statements about cookies is not true? ( ) \n\nOptions: \nA. Cookies are installed only at the user's request.\nB. Cookies are stored on the user's computer.\nC. Cookies cannot be easily detected or deleted.\nD. Cookies are used to support the user experience on websites.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let's evaluate each option:\n\nA. \"Cookies are installed only at the user's request\" – This is not true. While users can control cookie settings, cookies are often installed automatically when visiting websites, especially third-party tracking cookies, unless blocked by browser settings or consent mechanisms.\n\nB. Cookies are indeed stored on the user's computer – this is true.  \nC. While some users may not know how to detect or delete cookies, they can be easily managed through browser settings – so this is misleading, but the strongest false statement is A.  \nD. Cookies are commonly used to remember preferences and login states, supporting user experience – this is true.\n\nThe most clearly false statement is A.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
