add extra to bridges in the circular segment: from a to b-1 (inclusive)\n        low = a\n        high = b - 1\n        if high == 0:\n            high = N  # no, we want to handle modulo\n        # Actually, we don't set high=N, we handle wrapping.\n\n        if low <= high:\n            # range [low, high]\n            diff[low] += extra\n            diff[high+1] -= extra   # if high+1 <= N, else wrap\n        else:\n            # low > high: wrap around\n            # [low, N] and [1, high]\n            diff[low] += extra\n            diff[1] += extra\n            diff[high+1] -= extra   # if high+1 <= N, subtract at high+1\n            # if high+1 > N, then no subtract? but high <= N-1, so high+1<=N\n    else: # d_ccw < d_cw\n        # short path is counterclockwise from a to b\n        # equivalent to clockwise from b to a\n        low = b\n        high = a - 1\n        if high == 0:\n            high = N  # no, again, we handle by modulo arithmetic\n        # But if a==1, then a-1=0 → we want high = 0? but then we do [b, N] and [1,0] -> empty second part.\n\n        # Actually, if a==1, then high = 0, so we only do [b, N] if b<=N, which it is.\n\n        if low <= high:\n            if high >= 1:  # only if high>=1\n                diff[low] += extra\n                if high+1 <= N:\n                    diff[high+1] -= extra\n                # else if high==N, then we don't subtract? but we should use circular diff?\n            # else high==0, skip\n        else:\n            # low > high\n            if low <= N:\n                diff[low] += extra\n            diff[1] += extra\n            if high+1 <= N and high>=1:\n                diff[high+1] -= extra\n            # if high==0, then second part [1,0] is empty, so only do [low, N]\n\n   But wait, if high==0, then in the counterclockwise case, a==1, so we are going from a=1 to b counterclockwise: 1→N→N-1→...→b\n   The bridges: \n        from 1 to N: bridge N\n        from N to N-1: bridge N-1\n        ...