if key not in new_dp or new_dp[key] > new_cost:\n                    new_dp[key] = new_cost\n        dp = new_dp\n        if not dp:\n            break  # no way to cover\n    \n    if not dp:\n        print(-1)\n    else:\n        print(min(dp.values()))\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n```\n\nLet's test with the samples.\n\nSample 1: should output 17.\n\nWe can run locally.\n\nBut since we can't run here, we trust.\n\nSample 2: -1\n\nSample 3: 5\n\nWe'll submit.\n\nNote: We can add a check for empty dp during the loop.\n\nWe do.\n\nSo we call the function.\n\nBut the instruction: \"Simply call the function after the definition.\"\n\nWe do: `main()` is called if `__name__ == '__main__'`\n\nBut we can just call `main()`.\n\nBut it's fine.\n\nWe'll output the code as requested.\n\nNote: We assume that the input is as described.\n\nLet me write the final code.\n\nOne more thing: the range of `a` is from 0 to `K1`, inclusive.\n\nYes.\n\nWe use `K1+1` in range.\n\nYes.\n\nSo here is the code.",
