    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "I need to create a function that checks if a word is valid based on the given criteria.\n\nLet me break down the requirements:\n1. Minimum of 3 characters\n2. Only digits (0-9) and English letters (uppercase and lowercase)\n3. At least one vowel (a, e, i, o, u, A, E, I, O, U)\n4. At least one consonant (any English letter that is not a vowel)\n\nLet me think through the steps:\n1. Check if length is at least 3\n2. Check if all characters are digits or English letters (no special characters like '@', '#', '$')\n3. Check if there's at least one vowel\n4. Check if there's at least one consonant\n\n```python\ndef isValid(word):\n    # Check minimum length\n    if len(word) < 3:\n        return False\n    \n    # Define vowels\n    vowels = set('aeiouAEIOU')\n    \n    # Check if all characters are digits or English letters\n    for char in word:\n        if not (char.isalpha() or char.isdigit()):\n            return False\n    \n    # Check for at least one vowel and one consonant\n    has_vowel = False\n    has_consonant = False\n    \n    for char in word:\n        if char.isalpha():\n            if char in vowels:\n                has_vowel = True\n            else:\n                has_consonant = True\n    \n    return has_vowel and has_consonant\n```",
