t be covered.\n\nFor example, if we place A at (0,0): covers (0,0), (1,1)\n\nCan B cover (0,1)? Only if B's (0,0) or (1,1) is placed at (0,1).\n\nSay B's (0,0) → (0,1): dx=0, dy=1 → then (1,1) → (1,2) → invalid.\n\nB's (1,1) → (0,1): dx = -1, dy=0 → (0,0) → (-1,0) → r=-1 invalid.\n\nSimilarly for (1,0).\n\nSo B cannot contribute to (0,1) or (1,0).\n\nThus, union cannot include (0,1) or (1,0) → cannot match X.\n\nSo \"No\" — correct.\n\nBut wait, what if we place A to cover (0,0) and (1,1), and B to cover (0,1) and (1,0)? But B's pattern is diagonal, so it can't cover adjacent.\n\nSo impossible.\n\n---\n\n### **Sample 3**\n\nA: 1x1: '#' → black_A = [(0,0)]\n\nB: 1x2: '##' → black_B = [(0,0), (0,1)]\n\nX: 1x1: '#' → black_X = {(0,0)}\n\nNow, we need to place A and B such that:\n- A's black square (0,0) → (dxA, dyA) must be in [0,1) × [0,1) → so (0,0)\n- B's black squares: (0,0) and (0,1) must be in [0,1) × [0,1) → so both must go to (0,0) and (0,1)? But W_X=1 → c<1 → so c=0 only.\n\nSo (0,1) of B must go to (r, c) with c<1 → c=0? So dyB must be such that 0+dyB <1 and >=0 → dyB=0? Then (0,1) → (0,1) → c=1 >=1 → invalid.\n\nSo B's (0,1) cannot be placed in the cut-out.\n\nBut it must be included → impossible.\n\nSo no valid placement for B → no combination → \"No\".\n\nCorrect.\n\n---\n\n### **Sample 4**\n\nA: 3x3\n###\n...\n...\n\nblack_A = [(0,0), (0,1), (0,2)]\n\nB: 3x3\n#..\n#..\n#..\n\nblack_B = [(0,0), (1,0), (2,0)]\n\nX: 3x3\n..#\n..#\n###\n\nblack_X = {(0,2), (1,2), (2,0), (2,1), (2,2)}\n\nWe need to place A and B.\n\nSuppose we place A so that its row0 goes to row2: dxA=2, dyA=0 → then A_set = {(2,0), (2,1), (2,2)}\n\nPlace B so that its col0 goes to col2: dxB=0, dyB=2 → then B_set = {(0,2), (1,2), (2,2)}\n\nUnion = {(2,0), (2,1), (2,2), (0,2), (1,2)} → exactly black_X.\n\nAnd all positions in [0,3) × [0,3) → valid.\n\nSo \"Yes\".\n\nGood.\n\n---\n\n### **Code**\n\nWe'll use ranges for dx, dy from -10 to 20 (covers all possibilities given constraints).\n\n```python\ndef main():\n    import sys\n    data = sys.stdin.read().splitlines()\n    \n    # Read A\n    H_A, W_A = map(int, data[0].split())\n    A = data[1:1+H_A]\n    data = data[1+H_A:]\n    \n    # Read B\n    H_B, W_B = map(int, data[0].split())\n    B = data[1:1+H_B]\n    data = data[1+H_B:]\n    \n    # Read X\n    H_X, W_X = map(int, data[0].split())\n    X = data[1:1+H_X]\n    \n    # Extract black squares\n    black_A = []\n    for i in range(H_A):\n        for j in range(W_A):\n            if A[i][j] == '#':\n                black_A.append((i, j))\n                \n    black_B = []\n    for i in range(H_B):\n        for j in range(W_B):\n            if B[i][j] == '#':\n                black_B.append((i, j))\n                \n    black_X = set()\n    for i in range(H_X):\n        for j in range(W_X):\n            if X[i][j] == '#':\n                black_X.add((i, j))\n    \n    # Valid placements for A: (dx, dy) such that all black squares of A are in [0, H_X) x [0, W_X)\n    valid_A = []\n    for dx in range(-10, 20):\n        for dy in range(-10, 20):\n            valid = True\n            A_set = set()\n            for (r, c) in black_A:\n                nr, nc = r + dx, c + dy\n                if 0 <= nr < H_X and 0 <= nc < W_X:\n                    A_set.add((nr, nc))\n                else:\n                    valid = False\n                    break\n            if valid and A_set:  # at least one (but there is at least one black)\n                valid_A.append(A_set)\n    \n    # Valid placements for B\n    valid_B = []\n    for dx in range(-10, 20):\n        for dy in range(-10, 20):\n            valid = True\n            B_set = set()\n            for (r, c) in black_B:\n                nr, nc = r + dx, c + dy\n                if 0 <= nr < H_X and 0 <= nc < W_X:\n                    B_set.add((nr, nc))\n                else:\n                    valid = False\n                    break\n            if valid and B_set:\n                valid_B.append(B_set)\n    \n    # Check all combinations\n    for A_set in valid_A:\n        for B_set in valid_B:\n            union = A_set | B_set\n            if union == black_X:\n                print(\"Yes\")\n                return\n                \n    print(\"No\")\n\nmain()\n```\n\nBut note: we are storing only the set of positions, not the dx,dy — but that's fine.\n\nHowever, we are iterating over placements, but we don't need dx,dy in the combination.\n\nBut: could different dx,dy give same A_set? Yes, but we don't care.\n\nBut we might have duplicates. But with small sets, it's fine.\n\nAlternatively, we could use a set of frozensets, but not necessary.\n\nLet’s run with sample 1: should work.\n\nBut note: we are not storing dx,dy, but only the set — that's sufficient.\n\nBut wait: the same A_set might be generated multiple times — but it's okay, we can avoid by using set of frozensets, but not necessary for performance.\n\nBut to avoid duplicates, we can use:\n\n```python\nvalid_A_sets = set()\nfor ...:\n    if valid:\n        valid_A_sets.add(frozenset(A_set))\n```\n\nBut then we lose the ability to iterate easily, and duplicates won't hurt.\n\nBut let's keep as is.\n\nBut actually, we can do:\n\n```python\nvalid_A_sets = []\n...\nif valid:\n    valid_A_sets.append(A_set)\n```\n\nBut we might have duplicates. But 900×900 is acceptable.\n\nBut to be safe, we can use a set of frozensets.\n\nBut let's keep it simple.\n\nWait: what if no valid placement for A or B? Then valid_A or valid_B is empty → we print \"No\" — correct.\n\nLet me test with sample 3: B has two black squares, W_X=1, so B's (0,1) cannot be placed with c<1 → no valid placement for B → valid_B empty → no combination → \"No\" — correct.\n\nSo code should work.\n\nBut we can optimize by breaking early.\n\nBut not needed.\n\nLet me write the final code.\n\nNote: we are using `range(-10,20)` — since max H_X=10, and max coordinate in A is 9, so dx >= -9, and dx <= 10-1-0=9, so -10 to 20 is safe.\n\n---\n\n### **Final Code**\n\n\n```python\ndef main():\n    import sys\n    data = sys.stdin.read().splitlines()\n    \n    # Read A\n    H_A, W_A = map(int, data[0].split())\n    A = data[1:1+H_A]\n    idx = 1 + H_A\n    \n    # Read B\n    H_B, W_B = map(int, data[idx].split())\n    B = data[idx+1:idx+1+H_B]\n    idx = idx + 1 + H_B\n    \n    # Read X\n    H_X, W_X = map(int, data[idx].split())\n    X = data[idx+1:idx+1+H_X]\n    \n    # Extract black squares for A\n    black_A = []\n    for i in range(H_A):\n        for j in range(W_A):\n            if A[i][j] == '#':\n                black_A.append((i, j))\n                \n    # Extract black squares for B\n    black_B = []\n    for i in range(H_B):\n        for j in range(W_B):\n            if B[i][j] == '#':\n                black_B.append((i, j))\n                \n    # Extract black squares for X as a set\n    black_X = set()\n    for i in range(H_X):\n        for j in range(W_X):\n            if X[i][j] == '#':\n                black_X.add((i, j))\n    \n    # Generate all valid placements for A (only the resulting black positions in the cut-out)\n    valid_A = []\n    for dx in range(-10, 20):\n        for dy in range(-10, 20):\n            A_set = set()\n            valid = True\n            for (r, c) in black_A:\n                nr, nc = r + dx, c + dy\n                if 0 <= nr < H_X and 0 <= nc < W_X:\n                    A_set.add((nr, nc))\n                else:\n                    valid = False\n                    break\n            if valid and A_set:  # A_set non-empty (guaranteed by problem, but still)\n                valid_A.append(A_set)\n    \n    # Generate all valid placements for B\n    valid_B = []\n    for dx in range(-10, 20):\n        for dy in range(-10, 20):\n            B_set = set()\n            valid = True\n            for (r, c) in black_B:\n                nr, nc = r + dx, c + dy\n                if 0 <= nr < H_X and 0 <= nc < W_X:\n                    B_set.add((nr, nc))\n                else:\n                    valid = False\n                    break\n            if valid and B_set:\n                valid_B.append(B_set)\n    \n    # Check every combination\n    for A_set in valid_A:\n        for B_set in valid_B:\n            if A_set | B_set == black_X:\n                print(\"Yes\")\n                return\n                \n    print(\"No\")\n\nmain()\n```",
