\nAlternatively, we can store `root[i]` and update it lazily — but easier to just do iterative find.\n\nBut total operations $ O(N \\log N) $, so even $ O(\\log N) $ per find is acceptable.\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Implementation Plan\n\n```python\nMOD = 998244353\n\ndef mod_inv(a):\n    return pow(a, MOD-2, MOD)\n```\n\nSteps:\n\n1. Read N\n2. Initialize:\n   - `parent = list(range(N+1))`\n   - `comp = [[i] for i in range(N+1)]`  # comp[i] is list of players in component rooted at i (only valid for roots)\n   - `ans = [0]*(N+1)`\n3. For each of $ N-1 $ matches:\n   - Read $ p, q $\n   - `rp = find(p)`, `rq = find(q)`\n   - `A = comp[rp]`, `B = comp[rq]`\n   - `a = len(A)`, `b = len(B)`\n   - `total = a + b`\n   - `prob_A = a * mod_inv(total) % MOD`\n   - `prob_B = b * mod_inv(total) % MOD`\n   - For each `x in A`: `ans[x] = (ans[x] + prob_A) % MOD`\n   - For each `x in B`: `ans[x] = (ans[x] + prob_B) % MOD`\n   - Now merge: attach smaller tree to larger\n     - If `a >= b`:\n         - `parent[rq] = rp`\n         - `comp[rp] = A + B`\n         - `comp[rq] = []`  # invalidate\n     - Else:\n         - `parent[rp] = rq`\n         - `comp[rq] = A + B`\n         - `comp[rp] = []`\n4. Print `ans[1:]` as space separated\n\nBut note: when we do `find(p)`, we need to go to root. We don't do path compression, so it's just a loop.\n\nBut worst-case depth is $ O(N) $ if we don't balance. So we **must** use union by size (small-to-large) to keep depth low.\n\nBut even with small-to-large, the depth can be $ O(\\log N) $, which is acceptable.\n\nBut we are not storing parent tree for efficiency — we are only using parent to find root.\n\nSo we can write `find` as:\n\n```python\ndef find(x):\n    while parent[x] != x:\n        x = parent[x]\n    return x\n```\n\nBut we are merging roots, so only roots have `parent[x] == x`.\n\nYes.\n\n---\n\n### 🚫 Potential Performance Issue\n\nMerging lists with `A + B` creates a new list of size $ a + b $. With small-to-large, each player is moved $ O(