      "generated_answer": "We are given a **small** graph: $ N \\leq 8 $, so we can use **brute-force over all spanning trees**.\n\n---\n\n### 🔍 Problem Summary\n\n- We are given a **connected undirected weighted graph** with $ N \\leq 8 $ vertices.\n- We need to find a **spanning tree** (a connected acyclic subgraph with $ N-1 $ edges that covers all vertices).\n- The **cost** of a spanning tree is defined as:\n  $$\n  \\text{cost} = \\left( \\sum_{e \\in T} w_e \\right) \\mod K\n  $$\n- We are to **minimize this cost** (i.e., the **sum modulo K**, not the sum itself).\n\n⚠️ Important: We are **not minimizing the total sum**, but the **sum modulo K**. So even a large sum could yield a small value mod $ K $, and we want the **minimum possible value of (sum mod K)** over all spanning trees.\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Approach\n\nBecause $ N \\leq 8 $, the number of edges $ M \\leq \\frac{8 \\cdot 7}{2} = 28 $, and a spanning tree has exactly $ N-1 \\leq 7 $ edges.\n\nWe can:\n1. **Generate all possible subsets of $ N-1 $ edges**.\n2. For each subset:\n   - Check if it forms a **spanning tree** (i.e., connects all $ N $ vertices and has no cycles → i.e., forms a connected graph with $ N-1 $ edges).\n3. For valid spanning trees:\n   - Compute total weight $ S = \\sum w_i $\n   - Compute $ \\text{cost} = S \\mod K $\n4. Track the **minimum cost** over all spanning trees.\n\nWe can use:\n- `itertools.combinations` to generate all $ \\binom{M}{N-1} $ subsets of edges.\n- Union-Find (Disjoint Set Union) or DFS/BFS to check connectivity.\n\nBut since $ N \\leq 8 $ and $ M \\leq 28 $, even $ \\binom{28}{7} \\approx 1.2 \\times 10^6 $, which is acceptable in Python with optimizations.\n\n---\n\n### 🔧 Implementation Steps\n\n1. Read input.\n2. Precompute all combinations of $ N-1 $ edges.\n3. For each combination:\n   - Use Union-Find to:\n     - Check if the $ N-1 $ edges form a **tree** (i.e., no cycles during union, and finally all nodes are connected).\n   - If yes, compute total weight mod $ K $.\n4. Track the minimum such mod value.\n\n---\n\n### 📝 Important Notes\n\n- $ K $ can be up to $ 10^{15} $, but weights are less than $ K $, and at most 7 edges → total sum $ < 7K $, so mod is safe.\n- We are to **print the minimum value of (sum mod K)**, not the minimum sum.\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Code\n\n```python\nimport sys\nfrom itertools import combinations\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    \n    # Parse first three values\n    N = int(data[0]); M = int(data[1]); K = int(data[2])\n    \n    edges = []\n    index = 3\n    for i in range(M):\n        u = int(data[index]); v = int(data[index+1]); w = int(data[index+2])\n        index += 3\n        edges.append((u-1, v-1, w))  # Convert to 0-indexed vertices\n    \n    # If N == 1, then no edges needed, but N>=2 per constraints\n    from collections import defaultdict\n    \n    # Union-Find class for checking connectivity and cycles\n    class UnionFind:\n        def __init__(self, n):\n            self.parent = list(range(n))\n            self.rank = [0] * n\n            self.components = n\n        \n        def find(self, a):\n            if self.parent[a] != a:\n                self.parent[a] = self.find(self.parent[a])\n            return self.parent[a]\n        \n        def union(self, a, b):\n            pa = self.find(a)\n            pb = self.find(b)\n            if pa == pb:\n                return False  # already connected, cycle detected\n            if self.rank[pa] < self.rank[pb]:\n                self.parent[pa] = pb\n            elif self.rank[pa] > self.rank[pb]:\n                self.parent[pb] = pa\n            else:\n                self.parent[pb] = pa\n                self.rank[pa] += 1\n            self.components -= 1\n            return True\n        \n        def is_connected(self):\n            return self.components == 1\n    \n    min_cost = K  # will be at most K-1, so initialize to K\n    \n    # We need to consider all combinations of N-1 edges\n    from itertools import combinations\n    \n    for combo in combinations(edges, N-1):\n        uf = UnionFind(N)\n        total_weight = 0\n        valid = True\n        for u, v, w in combo:\n            total_weight += w\n            if not uf.union(u, v):\n                valid = False  # cycle detected\n                break\n        \n        if not valid:\n            continue\n        \n        if uf.is_connected():\n            cost = total_weight % K\n            if cost < min_cost:\n                min, we want minimum\n                min_cost = cost\n    \n    print(min_cost)\n\nmain()\n```\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Explanation of Key Points\n\n- We convert vertices to 0-indexed for easier array handling.\n- We use **Union-Find** to:\n  - Detect cycles (if an edge connects two already connected nodes → invalid).\n  - Check if final graph has one component (connected).\n- We iterate over all $ \\binom{M}{N-1} $ edge combinations.\n- For each valid spanning tree, compute $ \\text{sum} \\mod K $, and minimize it.\n\n---\n\n### 🧪 Sample Verification\n\n#### Sample 1:\n- N=5 → need 4 edges.\n- One valid combo: edges with weights 99,86,81,95 → sum = 361 → 361 mod 328 = 33 → correct.\n\n#### Sample 2:\n- Only one spanning tree possible (M = N-1 = 5), so must take all edges.\n- Sum = 337361568 + 450343304 + 61477244 + 745383438 + 727360840 = ?\n- But we can trust the code to compute mod $ K = 998244353 $.\n\nLet’s not recompute manually — code will do.\n\n---\n\n### 🚀 Final Code (Self-contained, executable)\n\n```python\nimport sys\nfrom itertools import combinations\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    N = int(data[0])\n    M = int(data[1])\n    K = int(data[2])\n    \n    edges = []\n    index = 3\n    for i in range(M):\n        u = int(data[index])\n        v = int(data[index+1])\n        w = int(data[index+2])\n        index += 3\n        edges.append((u-1, v-1, w))  # 0-indexed\n    \n    class UnionFind:\n        def __init__(self, n):\n            self.parent = list(range(n))\n            self.rank = [0] * n\n            self.components = n\n        \n        def find(self, a):\n            if self.parent[a] != a:\n                self.parent[a] = self.find(self.parent[a])\n            return self.parent[a]\n        \n        def union(self, a, b):\n            pa = self.find(a)\n            pb = self.find(b)\n            if pa == pb:\n                return False\n            if self.rank[pa] < self.rank[pb]:\n                self.parent[pa] = pb\n            elif self.rank[pa] > self.rank[pb]:\n                self.parent[pb] = pa\n            else:\n                self.parent[pb] = pa\n                self.rank[pa] += 1\n            self.components -= 1\n            return True\n        \n        def is_connected(self):\n            return self.components == 1\n\n    min_cost = K  # will be less than K\n    \n    for combo in combinations(edges, N-1):\n        uf = UnionFind(N)\n        total_weight = 0\n        valid = True\n        for u, v, w in combo:\n            total_weight += w\n            if not uf.union(u, v):\n                valid = False\n                break\n        if not valid:\n            continue\n        if uf.is_connected():\n            cost = total_weight % K\n            if cost < min_cost:\n                min_cost = cost\n\n    print(min_cost)\n\nmain()\n```\n\n---\n\n✅ This code will correctly solve the problem within feasible time for $ N \\leq 8 $.",
