se: a set with only one vertex? But K_i >= 2, so no.\n\nSo we are safe.\n\nLet’s write the code.\n\nNote: We are to read from stdin and print to stdout.\n\nWe'll define a DSU class or just functions. For simplicity, use arrays and functions.\n\nBut since we are in a script, we can use a class or just lists.\n\nWe'll do simple DSU with two lists: parent and rank.\n\n---\n\n### Final Code\n\n```python\nimport sys\n\nsys.setrecursionlimit(1 << 25)\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    \n    it = iter(data)\n    N = int(next(it)); M = int(next(it))\n    \n    operations = []\n    \n    for _ in range(M):\n        K = int(next(it)); C = int(next(it))\n        vertices = [int(next(it)) for _ in range(K)]\n        operations.append((C, vertices))\n    \n    # Sort by cost\n    operations.sort(key=lambda x: x[0])\n    \n    # DSU setup\n    parent = list(range(N+1))\n    rank = [0] * (N+1)\n    \n    def find(x):\n        if parent[x] != x:\n            parent[x] = find(parent[x])\n        return parent[x]\n    \n    def union(x, y):\n        rx = find(x)\n        ry = find(y)\n        if rx == ry:\n            return False\n        if rank[rx] < rank[ry]:\n            parent[rx] = ry\n        elif rank[rx] > rank[ry]:\n            parent[ry] = rx\n        else:\n            parent[ry] = rx\n            rank[rx] += 1\n        return True\n    \n    total_cost = 0\n    \n    for C, vertices in operations:\n        root = vertices[0]\n        for v in vertices[1:]:\n            if find(root) != find(v):\n                union(root, v)\n                total_cost += C\n    \n    # Check connectivity: all vertices 1 to N should have same root\n    root1 = find(1)\n    connected = True\n    for i in range(2, N+1):\n        if find(i) != root1:\n            connected = False\n            break\n    \n    if connected:\n        print(total_cost)\n    else:\n        print(-1)\n\nmain()\n```\n\nLet me test with sample 1 and 2 mentally — already did.\n\nThis should work.\n\nNote: We are using `find` with path compression, and union by rank — efficient.\n\nTotal operations: sum of (K_i - 1) <= sum of K_i <= 400,000 — very efficient.\n\nWe are good.\n\nNow output the code as required.",
