alid\n     - (2,1): red\n     - (2,3): invalid\n   - Only (1,2): C2 → $ k = 1 $\n   - $ f(c) = 2 - 1 + 1 = 2 $\n\nSum = 1 + 1 + 2 + 2 = 6  \nExpected = $ 6 / 4 = 3/2 $\n\nNow compute $ 3/2 \\mod 998244353 $\n\nWe need $ 3 \\times 2^{-1} \\mod 998244353 $\n\n$ 2^{-1} \\mod 998244353 = (998244353 + 1)//2 = 499122177 $?  \nActually: $ 2 \\times 499122177 = 998244354 \\equiv 1 \\mod 998244353 $\n\nSo $ 3 \\times 499122177 = 1497366531 \\mod 998244353 $\n\nCompute:\n1497366531 % 998244353 = ?\n\n998244353 * 1 = 998244353  \n1497366531 - 998244353 = 499122178\n\nSo answer = **499122178** → matches sample.\n\n---\n\n### **Code Implementation**\n\nWe’ll:\n- Use BFS for component labeling.\n- Use directions for neighbors.\n- Use a visited matrix for green cells.\n- Use a component ID grid.\n\nLet’s code accordingly.\n\n```python\nimport sys\nfrom collections import deque\n\nMOD = 998244353\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().splitlines()\n    H, W = map(int, data[0].split())\n    grid = [line.strip() for line in data[1:H+1]]\n    \n    # Directions for up, down, left, right\n    dx = [-1, 1, 0, 0]\n    dy = [0, 0, -1, 1]\n    \n    # Label green components\n    comp_id = [[-1] * W for _ in range(H)]  # -1: not green or not visited\n    comp_count = 0\n    visited = [[False] * W for _ in range(H)]\n    \n    for i in range(H):\n        for j in range(W):\n            if grid[i][j] == '#' and not visited[i][j]:\n                # BFS\n                queue = deque([(i, j)])\n                visited[i][j] = True\n                comp_id[i][j] = comp_count\n                while queue:\n                    x, y = queue.popleft()\n                    for d in range(4):\n                        nx, ny = x + dx[d], y + dy[d]\n                        if 0 <= nx < H and 0 <= ny < W and not visited[nx][ny] and grid[nx][ny] == '#':\n                            visited[nx][ny] = True\n                            comp_id[nx][ny] = comp_count\n                            queue.app