empty = K\n  - else:\n    - g = groups.pop(0)\n    - empty -= g\n\n- starts += 1\n\n- Print starts\n\nBut note: popping from front of list is O(n), but N <= 100, so it's fine.\n\nAlternatively, we can use index to avoid popping.\n\nBut for simplicity, we'll use list and pop(0).\n\nLet’s write the code accordingly.\n\n### Final Code:\n\n```python\nimport sys\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    n = int(data[0])\n    k = int(data[1])\n    A = list(map(int, data[2:2+n]))\n    \n    empty = k\n    starts = 0\n    groups = A[:]  # copy\n    \n    while groups:\n        if groups[0] > empty:\n            starts += 1\n            empty = k\n        else:\n            g = groups.pop(0)\n            empty -= g\n    \n    starts += 1\n    print(starts)\n\nmain()\n```\n\nBut wait — in the procedure, when we start the attraction, we **do not** remove the group. So we only remove it when we admit it.\n\nOur code does that: only pop when we admit.\n\nAnd when we start, we reset empty but keep the group.\n\nSo correct.\n\nLet’s run sample 1 again in code:\n\nA = [2,5,1,4,1,2,3], K=6\n\n- empty=6\n- 2 <=6 → pop → empty=4\n- 5 >4 → starts=1, empty=6\n- 5 <=6 → pop → empty=1\n- 1 <=1 → pop → empty=0\n- 4 >0 → starts=2, empty=6\n- 4 <=6 → pop → empty=2\n- 1 <=2 → pop → empty=1\n- 2 >1 → starts=3, empty=6\n- 2 <=6 → pop → empty=4\n- 3 <=4 → pop → empty=1\n- groups empty → starts +=1 → starts=4 → print 4 ✅\n\nSample 2: as above → 7 ✅\n\nSo we are confident.\n\nNow output the code as required.\n\nNote: The problem says \"Simply call the function after the definition.\"\n\nSo we define `main()` and call it.\n\nFinal answer:\n\n\n```python\nimport sys\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    n = int(data[0])\n    k = int(data[1])\n    A = list(map(int, data[2:2+n]))\n    \n    empty = k\n    starts = 0\n    groups = A\n    \n    while groups:\n        if groups[0] > empty:\n            starts += 1\n            empty = k\n        else:\n            g = groups.pop(0)\n            empty -= g\n    \n    starts += 1\n    print(starts)\n\nmain()\n```",
