    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "I need to find the length of the longest valid substring where no substring is in the forbidden list.\n\nLet me think through this step by step:\n\n1. A valid substring cannot contain any forbidden string as a substring\n2. I need to find the longest such substring in the given word\n3. The constraints suggest I need an efficient solution since word length can be up to 10^5\n\nMy approach:\n- Use a sliding window technique with two pointers (left and right)\n- For each position of the right pointer, expand the window\n- When I encounter a forbidden substring, I need to move the left pointer\n- However, I need to be careful about when to move the left pointer\n\nKey insight: Since forbidden strings can be up to length 10, when I find a forbidden substring ending at position r, I need to ensure my window doesn't contain it. The left pointer should be moved to at least one position after the start of this forbidden substring.\n\nBut there's a better approach:\n- For each ending position, I can check backwards up to 10 characters (since max forbidden length is 10)\n- If I find any forbidden substring ending at the current position, I need to adjust my window\n\nActually, let me use a two-pointer approach:\n- Keep expanding the right pointer\n- For each new character, check if adding it creates any forbidden substring ending at this position\n- If it does, move the left pointer to the maximum of its current position and (current position - forbidden_length + 1)\n- Track the maximum length seen so far\n\nWait, that's not quite right. If I find a forbidden substring of length L ending at position r, then any substring ending at r that starts at or before (r-L+1) is invalid. So I need to ensure my left pointer is at least (r-L+2).\n\nBut I need to consider all forbidden substrings that could end at position r.\n\nBetter approach:\n- Use two pointers: left and right\n- For each right position, check all substrings ending at right that have length <= 10 (since max forbidden length is 10)\n- If any of these substrings is in forbidden, then I need to move left to max(left, right - length + 2)\n- Update the maximum length\n\n```python\ndef longestValidSubstring(word, forbidden):\n    forbidden_set = set(forbidden)\n    left = 0\n    max_length = 0\n    \n    for right in range(len(word)):\n        # Check all possible forbidden substrings ending at position 'right'\n        # We only need to check substrings of length 1 to min(10, right - left + 1)\n        for length in range(1, min(10, right - left + 1) + 1):\n            start_pos = right - length + 1\n            substring = word[start_pos:right + 1]\n            if substring in forbidden_set:\n                left = max(left, start_pos + 1)\n                break\n        \n        max_length = max(max_length, right - left + 1)\n    \n    return max_length\n```",
