se `float('inf')` for simplicity.\n\nBut to avoid float, we can use a large integer.\n\nBut the problem says integers, so let's use `10**18`\n\n---\n\n### Code\n\n```python\nimport sys\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().splitlines()\n    if not data: \n        return\n    X, Y, Z = map(int, data[0].split())\n    S = data[1].strip()\n    \n    INF = 10**18\n    # dp0: min cost to be in state 0 (Caps Lock off)\n    # dp1: min cost to be in state 1 (Caps Lock on)\n    dp0 = 0\n    dp1 = INF  # cannot start in state 1\n    \n    for c in S:\n        # cost to type c in state 0\n        if c == 'a':\n            cost0 = X\n            cost1 = Y\n        else:  # c == 'A'\n            cost0 = Y\n            cost1 = X\n        \n        new_dp0 = min(dp0 + cost0, dp1 + Z + cost0)\n        new_dp1 = min(dp1 + cost1, dp0 + Z + cost1)\n        \n        dp0, dp1 = new_dp0, new_dp1\n    \n    print(min(dp0, dp1))\n\nmain()\n```\n\nLet’s run through sample 1 again:\n\nS = \"AAaA\"\n\nc = 'A': cost0 = Y=3, cost1 = X=1\n- new_dp0 = min(0+3, inf) = 3\n- new_dp1 = min(inf, 0 + Z + 1 = 3+1=4) = 4\n\nc = 'A': cost0=3, cost1=1\n- new_dp0 = min(3+3=6, 4+3+3=10) = 6\n- new_dp1 = min(4+1=5, 3+3+1=7) = 5\n\nc = 'a': cost0 = X=1, cost1 = Y=3\n- new_dp0 = min(6+1=7, 5+3+1=9) = 7\n- new_dp1 = min(5+3=8, 6+3+3=12) = 8\n\nc = 'A': cost0=3, cost1=1\n- new_dp0 = min(7+3=10, 8+3+3=14) = 10\n- new_dp1 = min(8+1=9, 7+3+1=11) = 9\n\nmin(10,9) = 9 → correct.\n\nAll samples should work.\n\nNow output the code as requested.\n\nNote: We assume exactly two lines of input.\n\nFinal code:\n\n\n```python\nimport sys\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().splitlines()\n    X, Y, Z = map(int, data[0].split())\n    S = data[1].strip()\n    \n    INF = 10**18\n    dp0 = 0         # cost ending with Caps Lock off\n    dp1 = INF       # cost ending with Caps Lock on\n    \n    for c in S:\n        if c == 'a':\n            cost_state0 = X   # press 'a' when Caps Off → 'a'\n            cost_state1 = 