      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef max_length_substring(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the maximum length of a substring such that it contains at most \n    two occurrences of each character.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n    max_len = 0\n    left = 0\n    counts = {}\n    \n    for right in range(n):\n        # Add the current character to the frequency map\n        char = s[right]\n        counts[char] = counts.get(char, 0) + 1\n        \n        # If the count exceeds 2, move the left pointer to shrink the window\n        # until the count of the character is at most 2\n        while counts[char] > 2:\n            left_char = s[left]\n            counts[left_char] -= 1\n            left += 1\n            \n        # Update the maximum length found so far\n        max_len = max(max_len, right - left + 1)\n        \n    return max_len\n```",
