y:\n     - \"acbfgh\" → no\n     - \"cbfgh\" → no\n     - \"bfgh\" → no\n     - \"fgh\" → yes → return index 0\n3. \"acbfegh\":\n   - try: \"acbfegh\", \"cbfegh\", \"bfegh\", \"fegh\", \"egh\", \"gh\" → \"gh\" is in map → index 2\n\n→ [2,0,2] → matches.\n\nPerfect.\n\n---\n\n### **Final Code**\n\nWe'll now write the function accordingly.\n\nNote: We must be careful about performance — but total suffixes is bounded.\n\n```python\ndef solve(wordsContainer, wordsQuery):\n    suffix_map = {}\n    \n    # Preprocess wordsContainer\n    for idx, word in enumerate(wordsContainer):\n        n = len(word)\n        # Generate all suffixes\n        for start in range(n + 1):\n            suff = word[start:]\n            curr_len = len(word)\n            if suff not in suffix_map:\n                suffix_map[suff] = (curr_len, idx)\n            else:\n                prev_len, prev_idx = suffix_map[suff]\n                if curr_len < prev_len or (curr_len == prev_len and idx < prev_idx):\n                    suffix_map[suff] = (curr_len, idx)\n    \n    ans = []\n    for q in wordsQuery:\n        found = False\n        for start in range(len(q) + 1):\n            suff = q[start:]\n            if suff in suffix_map:\n                ans.append(suffix_map[suff][1])\n                found = True\n                break\n        # Since \"\" is always present, we don't really need the else\n    return ans\n```\n\nBut the problem asks only for the **function body**, and not to invoke it.\n\nAlso, the function should be named appropriately.\n\nLet’s assume the function signature is:\n\n```python\ndef stringIndices(wordsContainer, wordsQuery):\n    # body\n```\n\nAnd return the list of indices.\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Final Answer\n\n```python\ndef stringIndices(wordsContainer, wordsQuery):\n    suffix_map = {}\n    \n    for idx, word in enumerate(wordsContainer):\n        n = len(word)\n        for start in range(n + 1):\n            suff = word[start:]\n            curr_len = len(word)\n  