      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve(words):\n    \"\"\"\n    To minimize the final length of the concatenated string, we can track the minimum length \n    achievable for each possible pair of (first_character, last_character) for the string \n    formed after each join operation.\n    \n    State:\n    dp[f][l] = the minimum length of the string formed so far, which starts with character 'f'\n               and ends with character 'l'.\n    \n    Transitions:\n    For each word in words[1:]:\n        For each state (f, l) from the previous step with length L:\n            New word has start_char 's' and end_char 'e' and length 'len_w'.\n            \n            Option 1: join(str_prev, word)\n                Resulting string starts with 'f', ends with 'e'.\n                New length is L + len_w - 1 if (l == s) else L + len_w.\n                \n            Option 2: join(word, str_prev)\n                Resulting string starts with 's', ends with 'l'.\n                New length is L + len_w - 1 if (e == f) else L + len_w.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not words:\n        return 0\n    \n    # dp[first_char][last_char] = min_length\n    # Using a dictionary for sparse state tracking\n    dp = {}\n    \n    # Initial state (from words[0])\n    first = words[0][0]\n    last = words[0][-1]\n    dp[(first, last)] = len(words[0])\n    \n    for i in range(1, len(words)):\n        next_word = words[i]\n        s = next_word[0]\n        e = next_word[-1]\n        len_w = len(next_word)\n        new_dp = {}\n        \n        for (f, l), length in dp.items():\n            # Option 1: join(str_prev, word)\n            # Starts with f, ends with e\n            added_len1 = len_w - 1 if l == s else len_w\n            new_len1 = length + added_len1\n            if (f, e) not in new_dp or new_len1 < new_dp[(f, e)]:\n                new_dp[(f, e)] = new_len1\n                \n            # Option 2: join(word, str_prev)\n            # Starts with s, ends with l\n            added_len2 = len_w - 1 if e == f else len_w\n            new_len2 = length + added_len2\n            if (s, l) not in new_dp or new_len2 < new_dp[(s, l)]:\n                new_dp[(s, l)] = new_len2\n        \n        dp = new_dp\n        \n    return min(dp.values())\n\n```",
