    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let's solve this step by step.\n\n### Step 1: Understand the setup\nWe have 7 points on a straight line: A, B, C, D, E, F, G, in that order.\n\nThe distances between adjacent points are:\n- A to B: 3\n- B to C: 1\n- C to D: 4\n- D to E: 1\n- E to F: 5\n- F to G: 9\n\nWe can compute the **positions** (coordinates) of each point by accumulating the distances from point A (which we can set at position 0).\n\n### Step 2: Assign coordinates\nLet’s assign coordinate 0 to point A.\n\nThen:\n- A: 0\n- B: 0 + 3 = 3\n- C: 3 + 1 = 4\n- D: 4 + 4 = 8\n- E: 8 + 1 = 9\n- F: 9 + 5 = 14\n- G: 14 + 9 = 23\n\nSo the positions are:\n```\nA: 0\nB: 3\nC: 4\nD: 8\nE: 9\nF: 14\nG: 23\n```\n\n### Step 3: Compute distance between any two points\nThe distance between two points is the **absolute difference** of their coordinates.\n\nFor example:\n- A to C: |0 - 4| = 4\n- G to B: |23 - 3| = 20\n- C to F: |4 - 14| = 10\n\n### Step 4: Map input to coordinates and compute\nWe are given two letters `p` and `q` as input (on one line, space-separated).\n\nWe need to:\n1. Read the input\n2. Map each letter to its coordinate\n3. Compute absolute difference\n4. Print the result\n\n### Step 5: Write the Python code\n\n```python\ndef main():\n    # Read input\n    p, q = input().split()\n    \n    # Define positions of each point\n    positions = {\n        'A': 0,\n        'B': 3,\n        'C': 4,\n        'D': 8,\n        'E': 9,\n        'F': 14,\n        'G': 23\n    }\n    \n    # Calculate distance\n    distance = abs(positions[p] - positions[q])\n    \n    # Output the result\n    print(distance)\n\nmain()\n```",
