      "generated_answer": "I'll solve this step by step.\n\n## Problem Understanding\n\n1. We need to check if a string satisfies a specific condition:\n   - The first character must be uppercase\n   - All other characters (if any) must be lowercase\n\n2. We need to read a string from stdin and output \"Yes\" if the condition is met, \"No\" otherwise.\n\n## Step-by-step Analysis\n\n1. **Check the first character**: It must be uppercase (A-Z)\n2. **Check the remaining characters**: All characters from index 1 to the end must be lowercase (a-z)\n3. **Edge case**: If the string has only one character, we only need to check if it's uppercase\n\n## Algorithm\n\n1. Read the input string S\n2. Check if the first character is uppercase\n3. Check if all characters from index 1 onwards are lowercase\n4. If both conditions are true, print \"Yes\", otherwise print \"No\"\n\n## Implementation\n\n```python\ndef solve():\n    S = input().strip()\n    \n    # Check if first character is uppercase\n    if not S[0].isupper():\n        print(\"No\")\n        return\n    \n    # Check if all other characters are lowercase\n    for i in range(1, len(S)):\n        if not S[i].islower():\n            print(\"No\")\n            return\n    \n    # If we reach here, both conditions are satisfied\n    print(\"Yes\")\n\nsolve()\n```\n\n## Verification with examples\n\n1. **\"Capitalized\"**: First char 'C' is uppercase, rest \"apitalized\" are lowercase → \"Yes\" ✓\n2. **\"AtCoder\"**: First char 'A' is uppercase, but 'C' at position 2 is uppercase → \"No\" ✓\n3. **\"yes\"**: First char 'y' is lowercase → \"No\" ✓\n4. **\"A\"**: Single character, 'A' is uppercase → \"Yes\" ✓\n\nThe solution correctly handles all test cases.",
