length=158+11=169, repeats=(169+11)//12=180//12=15 → 15*12=180 >=169 → ok.\n\nThen we check substrings. One starting at 0: 158 chars.\n\nAs computed: 13 full periods (156 chars): 91w,65b\n\nNext 2 chars: pattern[0]='w', pattern[1]='b' → +1w,1b → 92w,66b → match → prints \"Yes\"\n\nPerfect.\n\nSo final code:\n\nNote: We can simplify by just using a large enough repeat, but this is robust.\n\nLet’s write it.\n\nNote: We must not output anything else.\n\nFinal code:\n\n```python\ndef solve():\n    W, B = map(int, input().split())\n    total_len = W + B\n    pattern = \"wbwbwwbwbwbw\"\n    min_required_length = total_len + 11  # to cover all starting phases\n    repeats = (min_required_length + 11) // 12  # ceiling division: ceil(min_required_length / 12)\n    S_long = pattern * repeats\n    n = len(S_long)\n    for i in range(n - total_len + 1):\n        substr = S_long[i:i+total_len]\n        if substr.count('w') == W and substr.count('b') == B:\n            print(\"Yes\")\n            return\n    print(\"No\")\n\nsolve()\n```",
