      "generated_answer": "I need to find the minimum value of |x² + y² - D| for non-negative integers x and y.\n\nLet me think about this step by step:\n\n1. I need to find two non-negative integers x and y such that x² + y² is as close as possible to D.\n2. The minimum possible difference would be 0 if D can be expressed as the sum of two squares.\n3. Since D can be very large (up to 2×10¹²), I need an efficient approach.\n\nMy strategy:\n- I'll iterate through possible values of x from 0 to √D.\n- For each x, I'll find the best y such that x² + y² is closest to D.\n- For a fixed x, I want y² to be as close as possible to (D - x²).\n- The optimal y would be either floor(√(D - x²)) or ceil(√(D - x²)), whichever gives a sum closer to D.\n\nLet me implement this:\n\n```python\nimport math\n\ndef solve():\n    D = int(input().strip())\n    \n    min_diff = D  # Initialize with worst case (when x=y=0)\n    \n    # We only need to check x up to sqrt(D)\n    # Since x² <= D, x <= sqrt(D)\n    max_x = int(math.isqrt(D)) + 1\n    \n    for x in range(max_x + 1):\n        x_squared = x * x\n        if x_squared > D:\n            break\n            \n        remaining = D - x_squared\n        \n        # Find y such that y² is closest to remaining\n        if remaining == 0:\n            # x² = D, so y = 0 gives perfect match\n            y = 0\n            diff = abs(x_squared + y*y - D)\n            min_diff = min(min_diff, diff)\n        else:\n            # Find the integer y whose square is closest to remaining\n            y_sqrt = int(math.isqrt(remaining))\n            \n            # Check y_sqrt and y_sqrt + 1 (since we need non-negative integers)\n            for y in [y_sqrt, y_sqrt + 1]:\n                y_squared = y * y\n                total = x_squared + y_squared\n                diff = abs(total - D)\n                min_diff = min(min_diff, diff)\n                \n                # If we found a perfect match, we can return immediately\n                if diff == 0:\n                    print(0)\n                    return\n    \n    print(min_diff)\n\nsolve()\n```",
