    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport math\nfrom itertools import combinations\n\ndef nth_smallest_amount(coins, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the k^th smallest amount that can be made using multiples of \n    denominations in coins using binary search and the Principle of Inclusion-Exclusion.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    def get_lcm(a, b):\n        if a == 0 or b == 0:\n            return 0\n        return abs(a * b) // math.gcd(a, b)\n\n    # Precompute all non-empty subsets and their LCMs.\n    # subset_lcms will store tuples of (lcm_value, sign)\n    # where sign is 1 for odd subset sizes and -1 for even subset sizes.\n    subset_lcms = []\n    n = len(coins)\n    for i in range(1, 1 << n):\n        subset = []\n        for j in range(n):\n            if (i >> j) & 1:\n                subset.append(coins[j])\n        \n        lcm_val = subset[0]\n        for val in subset[1:]:\n            lcm_val = get_lcm(lcm_val, val)\n        \n        # Inclusion-Exclusion: \n        # Add if subset size is odd, subtract if even.\n        sign = 1 if len(subset) % 2 == 1 else -1\n        subset_lcms.append((lcm_val, sign))\n\n    def count_multiples(x):\n        count = 0\n        for lcm_val, sign in subset_lcms:\n            count += sign * (x // lcm_val)\n        return count\n\n    # Binary search for the k^th value.\n    # The smallest possible value is the minimum coin.\n    # A safe upper bound is k * min(coins).\n    low = min(coins)\n    high = k * min(coins)\n    ans = high\n    \n    while low <= high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if count_multiples(mid) >= k:\n            ans = mid\n            high = mid - 1\n        else:\n            low = mid + 1\n            \n    return ans\n\n```",
