      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef shortest_common_superstring(a: str, b: str, c: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the shortest string that contains a, b and c as substrings.\n    If several strings have the same minimum length, the lexicographically\n    smallest one is returned.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    from itertools import permutations\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------\n    # Helper: merge two strings into the shortest string that contains\n    # both as substrings (lexicographically smallest for equal length)\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------\n    def merge(s1: str, s2: str) -> str:\n        # one string already contains the other\n        if s2 in s1:\n            return s1\n        if s1 in s2:\n            return s2\n\n        best = s1 + s2                     # no overlap case\n\n        # s1 suffix overlaps s2 prefix\n        max_ov = min(len(s1), len(s2))\n        for i in range(1, max_ov + 1):\n            if s1[-i:] == s2[:i]:\n                cand = s1 + s2[i:]\n                if len(cand) < len(best) or (len(cand) == len(best) and cand < best):\n                    best = cand\n\n        # s2 suffix overlaps s1 prefix\n        for i in range(1, max_ov + 1):\n            if s2[-i:] == s1[:i]:\n                cand = s2 + s1[i:]\n                if len(cand) < len(best) or (len(cand) == len(best) and cand < best):\n                    best = cand\n\n        return best\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------\n    # Remove strings that are already substrings of another one\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------\n    strs = [a, b, c]\n    filtered = []\n    for s in strs:\n        if not any(s != t and s in t for t in strs):\n            filtered.append(s)\n\n    # If only one distinct string remains, it is already the answer\n    if len(filtered) == 1:\n        return filtered[0]\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------\n    # Try every permutation order and merge greedily;\n    # keep the best (shortest, then lexicographically smallest)\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------\n    best_answer = None\n    for order in permutations(filtered):\n        cur = order[0]\n        cur = merge(cur, order[1])\n        if len(filtered) == 3:\n            cur = merge(cur, order[2])\n\n        if (best_answer is None or\n            len(cur) < len(best_answer) or\n            (len(cur) == len(best_answer) and cur < best_answer)):\n            best_answer = cur\n\n    return best_answer\n```",
