bs(index_s[char] - index_t[char])\n    \n    return total_diff\n```\n\nWait, I can make this more concise:\n\n```python\ndef findPermutationDifference(s, t):\n    # Create a mapping of character to index for both strings\n    pos_s = {char: i for i, char in enumerate(s)}\n    pos_t = {char: i for i, char in enumerate(t)}\n    \n    # Sum the absolute differences\n    return sum(abs(pos_s[char] - pos_t[char]) for char in s)\n```\n\nThis is cleaner and does the same thing.\n\nLet me verify with the examples:\n\nExample 1: s = \"abc\", t = \"bac\"\n- pos_s: {'a': 0, 'b': 1, 'c': 2}\n- pos_t: {'b': 0, 'a': 1, 'c': 2}\n- For 'a': |0 - 1| = 1\n- For 'b': |1 - 0| = 1  \n- For 'c': |2 - 2| = 0\n- Total: 1 + 1 + 0 = 2 ✓\n\nExample 2: s = \"abcde\", t = \"edbac\"\n- pos_s: {'a': 0, 'b': 1, 'c': 2, 'd': 3, 'e': 4}\n- pos_t: {'e': 0, 'd': 1, 'b': 2, 'a': 3, 'c': 4}\n- For 'a': |0 - 3| = 3\n- For 'b': |1 - 2| = 1\n- For 'c': |2 - 4| = 2\n- For 'd': |3 - 1| = 2\n- For 'e': |4 - 0| = 4\n- Total: 3 + 1 + 2 + 2 + 4 = 12 ✓\n\nPerfect!\n\n```python\ndef findPermutationDifference(s, t):\n    pos_s = {char: i for i, char in enumerate(s)}\n    pos_t = {char: i for i, char in enumerate(t)}\n    return sum(abs(pos_s[char] - pos_t[char]) for char in s)\n```",
