ither is negative, return 0.\n\nLet:\n- $full\\_rows = r // N$\n- $full\\_cols = c // N$\n- $rem\\_r = r \\% N + 1$  → number of remaining rows (0..rem_r-1)\n- $rem\\_c = c \\% N + 1$  → number of remaining cols (0..rem_c-1)\n\nThen:\n- Number of complete tiles: $full\\_rows \\times full\\_cols$\n- Contribution from full tiles: $full\\_rows \\times full\\_cols \\times total\\_black$\n\nNow add:\n1. Remaining full-width part (bottom strip): full rows × partial columns → use prefix sum for first `rem_c` columns in each row of the base tile, summed over all rows, then over `full_cols` repetitions?\n   - Actually: sum over first `rem_c` columns for all $N$ rows → precompute `col_prefix`\n   - But better: use 2D prefix sum for arbitrary subrectangles\n\nSo let's build a 2D prefix sum array for the $N \\times N$ base pattern.\n\n---\n\n### 🛠️ **Preprocessing: 2D Prefix Sum**\n\nWe'll create a 2D array `pref` such that:\n```python\npref[i+1][j+1] = number of 'B' in P[0..i][0..j]\n```\n\nWe can then compute the number of black cells in any rectangle $(r1, c1)$ to $(r2, c2)$ (inclusive) in $O(1)$.\n\n---\n\n### 📐 **Decomposition of Region [0, r] × [0, c]**\n\nWe can split the region into:\n1. Full tiles: $ (r // N) \\times (c // N) $ tiles → contributes $full\\_rows \\times full\\_cols \\times total\\_black$\n2. Right partial strip: full rows of tiles, but only first $(c \\% N + 1)$ columns in last partial column of tiles\n   - Each row of base tile contributes: `sum of row[0..rem_c-1]`\n   - Sum over all $N$ rows → call this `sum_cols_up_to(rem_c-1)`\n   - Multiply by `full_rows`\n3. Bottom partial strip: only first $(r \\% N + 1)$ rows, full tile columns\n   - Sum over all columns for each of first `rem_r` rows → `sum_rows_up_to(rem_r-1)`\n   - Multiply by `full_cols`\n4. Bottom-right leftover corner: rectangle of size `rem_r × rem_c` in the base tile → use prefix sum\n\nBut wait — actually, the right strip is not over all N rows but only the partial block. We can do it cleanly using the prefix function.\n\nAlternatively, define a helper:\n\n```python\ndef query_tile(r1, c1, r2, c2):\n    # number of black cells in base tile from (r1,c1) to (r2,c2) inclusive\n    # using pref array\n```\n\nThen:\n\n```python\nfull_rows = r // N\nfull_cols = c // N\nrem_r = r % N\nrem_c = c % N\n\ntotal = 0\ntotal += full_rows * full_cols * total_black\n\n# Top-right partial strip (right part, full row tiles)\nif full_rows > 0 and rem_c >= 0:\n    # Each full row of tiles contributes sum of [0:N, 0:rem_c]\n    total += full_rows * query_tile(0, 0, N-1, rem_c)\n\n# Bottom full-width strip (bottom part, full col tiles)\nif full_cols > 0 and rem_r >= 0:\n    # Each full col of tiles contributes sum of [0:rem_r, 0:N-1]\n    total += full_cols * query_tile(0, 0, rem_r, N-1)\n\n# Bottom-right small corner\nif rem_r >= 0 and rem_c >= 0:\n    total += query_tile(0, 0, rem_r, rem_c)\n\nreturn total\n```\n\nWait — this overcounts?\n\nActually, the standard way is:\n\nWe want to compute number of black cells in $[0, r] \\times [0, c]$.\n\nLet:\n- $R = r + 1$, $C = c + 1$\n- $full\\_rows = R // N$, $rem\\_r = R \\% N$\n- $full\\_cols = C // N$, $rem\\_c = C \\% N$\n\nBut since indexing is from 0, better to think in blocks.\n\nActually, here's a clean method:\n\nLet’s define:\n\n```python\ndef count_rect(r1, c1, r2, c2):\n    # Count black cells from (r1, c1) to (r2, c2) inclusive\n    # Decompose into full and partial tiles\n    # But we'll instead use inclusion-exclusion via [0,0] to [r,c]\n```\n\nBut we already decided to use:\n\n```python\nans = f(C, D) - f(A-1, D) - f(C, B-1) + f(A-1, B-1)\n```\n\nSo define `f(r, c)` = number of black cells in $[0, r] \\times [0, c]$\n\nIf $r < 0$ or $c < 0$, return 0.\n\nOtherwise:\n\n- $full\\_rows = r // N$ → number of complete repetitions in rows\n- $full\\_cols = c // N$ → same for columns\n- $r\\_end = r \\% N$  → last row index in base tile\n- $c\\_end = c \\% N$  → last col index in base tile\n\nThen:\n\n1. Full blocks: `full_rows * full_cols * total_black`\n2. Right strip: `full_rows * (number of black cells in base tile rows [0, N-1], cols [0, c_end])`\n3. Bottom strip: `full_cols * (number of black cells in base tile rows [0, r_end], cols [0, N-1])`\n4. Bottom-right corner: `number of black cells in base tile [0, r_end] x [0, c_end]`\n\nSo we need a function to compute the sum of a subrectangle in the base tile.\n\nWe'll build a 2D prefix sum array `pref` of size $(N+1) \\times (N+1)$\n\n```python\npref[i+1][j+1] = sum_{x=0}^{i} sum_{y=0}^{j} (1 if P[x][y]=='B' else 0)\n```\n\nThen:\n\n```python\ndef get_sum(r1, c1, r2, c2):\n    # returns sum in rectangle [r1, r2] x [c1, c2] inclusive\n    if r1 > r2 or c1 > c2:\n        return 0\n    return pref[r2+1][c2+1] - pref[r1][c2+1] - pref[r2+1][c1] + pref[r1][c1]\n```\n\nBut in our case, we always go from (0,0), so we can define:\n\n```python\ndef tile_sum_to(r, c):\n    if r < 0 or c < 0:\n        return 0\n    return pref[r+1][c+1]\n```\n\nSo now:\n\n```python\ndef f(r, c):\n    if r < 0 or c < 0:\n        return 0\n    full_rows = r // N\n    full_cols = c // N\n    rem_r = r % N\n    rem_c = c % N\n\n    total = 0\n    # Full tiles\n    total += full_rows * full_cols * total_black\n\n    # Right strip: full rows, last partial column\n    if full_rows > 0:\n        total += full_rows * tile_sum_to(N-1, rem_c)\n\n    # Bottom strip: full cols, last partial row\n    if full_cols > 0:\n        total += full_cols * tile_sum_to(rem_r, N-1)\n\n    # Bottom-right corner\n    total += tile_sum_to(rem_r, rem_c)\n\n    return total\n```\n\nWait — this **overcounts** the bottom-right corner? No, because:\n- The right strip is: `[0, N-1] x [0, rem_c]` repeated `full_rows` times → covers columns in full row blocks\n- The bottom strip is: `[0, rem_r] x [0, N-1]` repeated `full_cols` times\n- But the corner `[0, rem_r] x [0, rem_c]` is added once at the end\n\nBut actually, the above decomposition is **not** correct.\n\nThe correct way:\n\nThe region `[0, r] x [0, c]` can be broken into:\n\n1. `[0, full_rows*N - 1] x [0, full_cols*N - 1]` → full tiles: count = `full_rows * full_cols * total_black`\n\n2. Remaining parts:\n   a. Vertical strip: `[0, full_rows*N - 1] x [full_cols*N, c]`\n   b. Horizontal strip: `[full_rows*N, r] x [0, full_cols*N - 1]`\n   c. Corner: `[full_rows*N, r] x [full_cols*N, c]`\n\nWe can compute each using the base tile.\n\nLet’s define:\n- `start_r = full_rows * N`\n- `start_c = full_cols * N`\n\nBut since the pattern is periodic, the value at `(i, j)` depends on `(i % N, j % N)`.\n\nSo:\n\n- The vertical strip: has `full_rows * N` rows → `full_rows` full repetitions of base rows\n   - The column range: from `start_c` to `c` → length = `rem_c + 1`, but starting at column `full_cols*N`, so column indices mod N: from 0 to `rem_c`? No!\n\nWait: `c = full_cols * N + rem_c`, so the partial columns are from `full_cols*N` to `full_cols*N + rem_c`, which mod N is from 0 to `rem_c`.\n\nSimilarly for rows.\n\nSo:\n\n- Vertical strip: for each row in `[0, full_rows*N - 1]`, we are summing over columns `[0, rem_c]` in the base tile.\n   - Each base row `x` contributes: number of black cells in row `x` from col 0 to `rem_c`\n   - Sum over all base rows: `S1 = sum_{x=0}^{N-1} (number of 'B' in P[x][0..rem_c])`\n   - There are `full_rows` full repetitions of the base tile in rows → total = `full_rows * S1`\n\nSimilarly:\n- Horizontal strip: for each column in `[0, full_cols*N - 1]`, sum over rows `[0, rem_r]` in base tile\n   - Each base column `y` contributes: sum of `P[0..rem_r][y]`\n   - Total over all base columns: `S2 = sum_{y=0}^{N-1} (number of 'B' in P[0..rem_r][y])`\n   - Multiply by `full_cols`\n\n- Corner: `[0, rem_r] x [0, rem_c]` in base tile → just `tile_sum_to(rem_r, rem_c)`\n\nSo we need:\n- `col_sum_to(c)` = sum over all rows, columns 0 to c → `tile_sum_to(N-1, c)`\n- `row_sum_to(r)` = sum over all cols, rows 0 to r → `tile_sum_to(r, N-1)`\n\nSo the function becomes:\n\n```python\ndef f(r, c):\n    if r < 0 or c < 0:\n        return 0\n    full_rows = r // N\n    full_cols = c // N\n    rem_r = r % N\n    rem_c = c % N\n\n    total = 0\n\n    # Full blocks\n    total += full_rows * full_cols * total_black\n\n    # Right vertical strip: [0, full_rows*N - 1] x [full_cols*N, c]\n    if full_cols <= c // N:  # meaning there is a partial column block\n        # columns mod: 0 to rem_c\n        col_block_sum = tile_sum_to(N-1, rem_c)  # sum over all rows, first rem_c+1 cols\n        total += full_rows * col_block_sum\n\n    # Bottom horizontal strip: [full_rows*N, r] x [0, full_cols*N - 1]\n    row_block_sum = tile_sum_to(rem_r, N-1)  # sum over first rem_r+1 rows, all cols\n    total += full_cols * row_block_sum\n\n    # Bottom-right corner: [full_rows*N, r] x [full_cols*N, c]\n    corner_sum = tile_sum_to(rem_r, rem_c)\n    total += corner_sum\n\n    return total\n```\n\nWait — the horizontal strip: we multiply by `full_cols`, yes, because there are `full_cols` full repetitions of the base tile in columns.\n\nYes.\n\nBut note: the vertical strip uses `full_rows` repetitions, each contributing a full column of base tiles (N rows), so we multiply `full_rows * col_block_sum`.\n\nYes.\n\nNow, answer for a query `(A, B, C, D)` is:\n\n```python\nf(C, D) - f(A-1, D) - f(C, B-1) + f(A-1, B-1)\n```\n\nThis is standard 2D inclusion-exclusion.\n\n---\n\n### ✅ **Implementation Steps**\n\n1. Read $N, Q$\n2. Read $N$ lines of $N$ characters\n3. Build a 2D prefix sum array `pref` of size $(N+1) \\times (N+1)$\n4. Precompute `total_black = pref[N][N]`\n5. Define `tile_sum_to(r, c)` which returns `pref[r+1][c+1]` (if r,c >=0)\n6. Define `f(r, c)` as above\n7. For each query `(A, B, C, D)`, compute:\n   ```python\n   ans = f(C, D) - f(A-1, D) - f(C, B-1) + f(A-1, B-1)\n   ```\n\n---\n\n### 💡 Edge Cases\n\n- `A-1` or `B-1` can be -1 → `f(-1, x) = 0`, `f(x, -1) = 0`\n- `r % N` and `c % N` are in $[0, N-1]$\n\n---\n\n### 🧪 Let's Test on Sample 1\n\nInput:\n```\n3 2\nWWB\nBBW\nWBW\n1 2 3 4\n0 3 4 5\n```\n\nBuild `P`:\n```\nP[0] = 'WWB' → [W,W,B]\nP[1] = 'BBW' → [B,B,W]\nP[2] = 'WBW' → [W,B,W]\n```\n\nBuild `pref` (size 4x4):\n\n```\npref[i+1][j+1] = sum up to (i,j)\n```\n\nCompute manually:\n\nRow 0: W W B → 0 0 1 → prefix: 0,0,1\nRow 1: B B W → 1 1 0 → prefix: 1,2,2\nRow 2: W B W → 0 1 0 → prefix: 0,1,1\n\nNow build 2D prefix:\n\n```\npref[1][1] = (0,0) = 0\npref[1][2] = 0\npref[1][3] = 1\n\npref[2][1] = (0,0)+(1,0) = 0+1 = 1\npref[2][2] = 0+0+1+1 = 2\npref[2][3] = 0+0+1 +1+1+0 = 3\n\npref[3][1] = col0: 0+1+0 = 1\npref[3][2] = \n(0,0):0, (0,1):0\n(1,0):1, (1,1):1\n(2,0):0, (2,1):1 → total = 0+0+1+1+0+1 = 3\nActually better to build step by step.\n\nLet me build `pref` array properly:\n\nInitialize (4x4) with 0.\n\nFor i in 0..2, j in 0..2:\n  val = 1 if P[i][j]=='B' else 0\n  pref[i+1][j+1] = val + pref[i][j+1] + pref[i+1][j] - pref[i][j]\n\nSo:\n\ni=0:\n  j=0: W → 0 → pref[1][1] = 0\n  j=1: W → 0 → pref[1][2] = 0+0+0-0=0\n  j=2: B → 1 → pref[1][3] = 1 + pref[1][2] (0) + pref[0][3] (0) - pref[0][2] (0) → 1\n\ni=1:\n  j=0: B →1 → pref[2][1] = 1 + pref[1][1] (0) + pref[2][0] (0) - pref[1][0] (0) → 1\n  j=1: B →1 → pref[2][2] = 1 + pref[1][2] (0) + pref[2][1] (1) - pref[1][1] (0) → 1+0+1-0=2\n  j=2: W →0 → pref[2][3] = 0 + pref[1][3] (1) + pref[2][2] (2) - pref[1][2] (0) → 0+1+2-0=3\n\ni=2:\n  j=0: W →0 → pref[3][1] = 0 + pref[2][1] (1) + pref[3][0] (0) - pref[2][0] (0) → 1\n  j=1: B →1 → pref[3][2] = 1 + pref[2][2] (2) + pref[3][1] (1) - pref[2][1] (1) → 1+2+1-1=3\n  j=2: W →0 → pref[3][3] = 0 + pref[2][3] (3) + pref[3][2] (3) - pref[2][2] (2) → 0+3+3-2=4\n\nSo `pref`:\nRow0: 0 0 0 0\nRow1: 0 0 0 1\nRow2: 0 1 2 3\nRow3: 0 1 3 4\n\nSo `total_black = pref[3][3] = 4`\n\nNow first query: A=1, B=2, C=3, D=4\n\nWe want black cells in rectangle from (1,2) to (3,4)\n\nCompute:\n```\nans = f(3,4) - f(0,4) - f(3,1) + f(0,1)\n```\n\nLet’s compute each:\n\n---\n\n**f(3,4)**\n\nr=3, c=4\nfull_rows = 3 // 3 = 1, rem_r = 0\nfull_cols = 4 // 3 = 1, rem_c = 1\n\ntotal = 0\n- full blocks: 1*1*4 = 4\n- vertical strip: full_rows * tile_sum_to(N-1, rem_c) = 1 * tile_sum_to(2,1) = pref[3][2] = 3\n- horizontal strip: full_cols * tile_sum_to(rem_r, N-1) = 1 * tile_sum_to(0,2) = pref[1][3] = 1\n- corner: tile_sum_to(0,1) = pref[1][2] = 0\n→ total = 4 + 3 + 1 + 0 = 8\n\nWait, that seems high.\n\nWait: tile_sum_to(r,c) = pref[r+1][c+1]\n\nSo:\n- tile_sum_to(2,1) = pref[3][2] = 3 → correct (sum of first 3 rows, first 2 cols: (0,0):0, (0,1):0, (1,0):1, (1,1):1, (2,0):0, (2,1):1 → total 3)\n- tile_sum_to(0,2) = pref[1][3] = 1 → row0, col0-2: only (0,2) is B → 1\n- tile_sum_to(0,1) = pref[1][2] = 0\n\nSo f(3,4)=8\n\n---\n\n**f(0,4)**\n\nr=0, c=4\nfull_rows = 0 // 3 = 0, rem_r = 0\nfull_cols = 4 // 3 = 1, rem_c = 1\n\n- full blocks: 0\n- vertical strip: 0 * ... = 0\n- horizontal strip: 1 * tile_sum_to(0,2) = 1 * 1 = 1\n- corner: tile_sum_to(0,1) = 0\n→ total = 1\n\n---\n\n**f(3,1)**\n\nr=3, c=1\nfull_rows = 1, rem_r=0\nfull_cols = 1 // 3 = 0, rem_c=1\n\n- full: 0\n- vertical: 1 * tile_sum_to(2,1) = 1*3 = 3\n- horizontal: 0\n- corner: tile_sum_to(0,1) = 0\n→ total = 3\n\n---\n\n**f(0,1)**\n\nr=0, c=1\nfull_rows=0, full_cols=0\n→ only corner: tile_sum_to(0,1)=0\n\nSo:\nans = 8 - 1 - 3 + 0 = 4 → ✅ matches\n\n---\n\nSecond query: A=0, B=3, C=4, D=5\n\nSo:\nans = f(4,5) - f(-1,5) - f(4,2) + f(-1,2)\nf(-1,x)=0, so:\nans = f(4,5) - f(4,2)\n\nCompute f(4,5):\n\nr=4, c=5\nfull_rows = 4//3=1, rem_r=1\nfull_cols=5//3=1, rem_c=2\n\n- full: 1*1*4=4\n- vertical: 1 * tile_sum_to(2,2) = pref[3][3]=4\n- horizontal: 1 * tile_sum_to(1,2) = pref[2][3]=3\n- corner: tile_sum_to(1,2)=pref[2][3]=3\n→ total = 4 + 4 + 3 + 3 = 14\n\nf(4,2):\n\nr=4, c=2\nfull_rows=1, rem_r=1\nfull_cols=2//3=0, rem_c=2\n\n- full: 0\n- vertical: 1 * tile_sum_to(2,2)=4\n- horizontal: 0\n- corner: tile_sum_to(1,2)=3\n→ total = 4 + 3 = 7\n\nans = 14 - 7 = 7 → ✅\n\nPerfect.\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Final Code\n\n```python\nimport sys\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().splitlines()\n    if not data: \n        return\n    \n    N, Q = map(int, data[0].split())\n    P = []\n    for i in range(1, 1+N):\n        P.append(data[i].strip())\n    \n    # Build prefix sum: pref[i+1][j+1] = sum from (0,0) to (i,j)\n    pref = [[0]*(N+1) for _ in range(N+1)]\n    for i in range(N):\n        for j in range(N):\n            val = 1 if P[i][j] == 'B' else 0\n            pref[i+1][j+1] = val + pref[i][j+1] + pref[i+1][j] - pref[i][j]\n    \n    total_black = pref[N][N]\n    \n    def tile_sum_to(r, c):\n        # sum from (0,0) to (r,c) in base tile\n        if r < 0 or c < 0:\n            return 0\n        r = min(r, N-1)\n        c = min(c, N-1)\n        return pref[r+1][c+1]\n    \n    def f(r, c):\n        # number of black cells in [0, r] x [0, c]\n        if r < 0 or c < 0:\n            return 0\n        full_rows = r // N\n        full_cols = c // N\n        rem_r = r % N\n        rem_c = c % N\n        \n        total = 0\n        # Full tiles\n        total += full_rows * full_cols * total_black\n        \n        # Right vertical strip: [0, full_rows*N - 1] x [full_cols*N, c]\n        # This corresponds to full_rows repetitions of base tile in rows, and columns 0 to rem_c\n        if full_rows > 0:\n            col_block = tile_sum_to(N-1, rem_c)  # all rows, cols 0..rem_c\n            total += full_rows * col_block\n        \n        # Bottom horizontal strip: [full_rows*N, r] x [0, full_cols*N - 1]\n        # full_cols repetitions of base tile in columns, rows 0 to rem_r\n        if full_cols > 0:\n            row_block = tile_sum_to(rem_r, N-1)  # rows 0..rem_r, all cols\n            total += full_cols * row_block\n        \n        # Bottom-right corner: [full_rows*N, r] x [full_cols*N, c]\n        corner = tile_sum_to(rem_r, rem_c)\n        total += corner\n        \n        return total\n    \n    out_lines = []\n    for i in range(1+N, 1+N+Q):\n        A, B, C, D = map(int, data[i].split())\n        res = f(C, D) - f(A-1, D) - f(C, B-1) + f(A-1, B-1)\n        out_lines.append(str(res))\n    \n    print(\"\\n\".join(out_lines))\n\nmain()\n```\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Final Output Format\n\nThe function reads from stdin, processes input, and prints answers line by line.\n\nWe call `main()` at the end.\n\nThis handles all constraints:\n- $N \\leq 1000$: prefix sum is $O(N^2)$\n- $Q \\leq 2\\times10^5$: each query $O(1)$\n\nLet's run with the samples — already verified.\n\n---\n\n✅ **Done.**",
