by 3? 8+5+2=15 → yes → bus at 852 → arrive at 853\n- walk → 856\n\nYes! matches.\n\nSo the method is correct.\n\n---\n\n### Implementation Steps:\n\n1. Read N, X, Y\n2. Read N-1 lines of P_i, T_i → store in list `buses`\n3. Precompute `F` for `r` in `0` to `839`:\n   - For each `r`, simulate the journey from stop 1 at time `r` to Aoki's house.\n4. Read Q\n5. For each query `q`:\n   - `t1 = q + X`\n   - `k = t1 // 840`\n   - `r = t1 % 840`\n   - `ans = F[r] + k * 840`\n   - Print `ans`\n\n---\n\n### Edge: F[r] might be very large? But that's okay.\n\nWe are using integers.\n\nLet’s code accordingly.\n\nNote: We must simulate the bus rides carefully.\n\n---\n\nLet’s write the code accordingly.\n\n```python\ndef main():\n    import sys\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    \n    # Parse first line\n    it = iter(data)\n    N = int(next(it)); X = int(next(it)); Y = int(next(it))\n    \n    buses = []\n    for _ in range(N-1):\n        P = int(next(it)); T = int(next(it))\n        buses.append((P, T))\n    \n    Q = int(next(it))\n    queries = [int(next(it)) for _ in range(Q)]\n    \n    period = 840\n    F = [0] * period  # F[r] = arrival time at Aoki's house if arrive at stop 1 at time r\n    \n    # Precompute F[r] for r in 0 to 839\n    for r in range(period):\n        t = r\n        for P, T in buses:\n            # Compute next departure time: smallest multiple of P >= t\n            if t % P == 0:\n                departure = t\n            else:\n                departure = (t // P + 1) * P\n            t = departure + T\n        t += Y\n        F[r] = t\n    \n    # Process queries\n    for q in queries:\n        t1 = q + X  # arrival time at stop 1\n        k = t1 // period\n        r = t1 % period\n        ans = F[r] + k * period\n        print(ans)\n\nmain()\n```\n\nLet’s test with sample.\n\nWe already tested q=13 and q=0.\n\nq=13: t1=15 → r=15, k=0 → F[15]=34 → prints 34.\n\nq=0: t1=2 → r=2 → F[2]=22 → prints 22.\n\nNe