      "generated_answer": "I need to solve this step by step.\n\nThe problem asks for the punishment number of n, which is the sum of squares of all integers i (from 1 to n) where the decimal representation of i*i can be partitioned into contiguous substrings that sum to i.\n\nLet me break this down:\n1. For each i from 1 to n, I need to check if i*i (the square) can be partitioned into substrings\n2. The sum of the integer values of these substrings should equal i\n3. If it satisfies the condition, add i*i to the result\n\nFor the partitioning part, I need to check all possible ways to split the string representation of i*i into contiguous substrings and see if any partition sums to i.\n\nLet me trace through the examples:\n- i = 1: 1*1 = 1, and 1 = 1 ✓\n- i = 9: 9*9 = 81, and 8 + 1 = 9 ✓\n- i = 10: 10*10 = 100, and 10 + 0 = 10 ✓\n- i = 36: 36*36 = 1296, and 1 + 29 + 6 = 36 ✓\n\nTo check if a number satisfies the condition, I need a recursive function that tries all possible partitions of the string representation of i*i.\n\nHere's my approach:\n1. For each i from 1 to n:\n   - Calculate square = i * i\n   - Convert square to string\n   - Use recursion/backtracking to check if we can partition this string such that the sum equals i\n2. If yes, add square to the result\n\nThe recursive function will try all possible ways to split the string from the current position and check if any partition leads to the target sum.\n\n```python\ndef punishmentNumber(n):\n    def can_partition(s, target, current_sum=0, start=0):\n        # If we've processed the entire string\n        if start == len(s):\n            return current_sum == target\n        \n        # Try all possible substrings starting from 'start'\n        for end in range(start + 1, len(s) + 1):\n            # Extract substring and convert to integer\n            substring_value = int(s[start:end])\n            # Recursively check the rest of the string\n            if can_partition(s, target, current_sum + substring_value, end):\n                return True\n        return False\n    \n    total = 0\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        square = i * i\n        square_str = str(square)\n        if can_partition(square_str, i):\n            total += square\n    \n    return total\n```",
