      "generated_answer": "```python\n\ndef minimumCost(source, target, original, changed, cost):\n    INF = 10**18\n    # distance matrix for letters 'a'..'z' (indices 0..25)\n    dist = [[INF] * 26 for _ in range(26)]\n    for i in range(26):\n        dist[i][i] = 0\n\n    # add given direct transformations\n    for o, c, w in zip(original, changed, cost):\n        u = ord(o) - ord('a')\n        v = ord(c) - ord('a')\n        if w < dist[u][v]:\n            dist[u][v] = w\n\n    # Floyd‑Warshall to compute all‑pairs shortest paths\n    for k in range(26):\n        for i in range(26):\n            if dist[i][k] == INF:\n                continue\n            for j in range(26):\n                if dist[k][j] == INF:\n                    continue\n                nd = dist[i][k] + dist[k][j]\n                if nd < dist[i][j]:\n                    dist[i][j] = nd\n\n    total = 0\n    for s, t in zip(source, target):\n        u = ord(s) - ord('a')\n        v = ord(t) - ord('a')\n        d = dist[u][v]\n        if d == INF:\n            return -1\n        total += d\n    return total\n\n```",
