    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "I need to create a function that checks if a 3-digit number is \"fascinating\" based on the given conditions.\n\nLet me break down the requirements:\n1. Take a 3-digit number n\n2. Concatenate n with 2*n and 3*n\n3. Check if the resulting number contains all digits from 1 to 9 exactly once and has no 0's\n4. Return True if fascinating, False otherwise\n\nStep-by-step approach:\n1. Calculate 2*n and 3*n\n2. Concatenate n, 2*n, and 3*n as strings\n3. Check if the concatenated string has exactly 9 digits\n4. Check if it contains all digits 1-9 exactly once (no 0's allowed)\n\n```python\ndef isFascinating(n):\n    # Calculate 2*n and 3*n\n    double_n = 2 * n\n    triple_n = 3 * n\n    \n    # Concatenate n, 2*n, and 3*n as strings\n    concatenated = str(n) + str(double_n) + str(triple_n)\n    \n    # Check if the length is 9 (should contain exactly 9 digits)\n    if len(concatenated) != 9:\n        return False\n    \n    # Check if it contains all digits from 1 to 9 exactly once and no 0's\n    # Create a set of expected digits (1-9)\n    expected_digits = set('123456789')\n    \n    # Create a set of actual digits in the concatenated string\n    actual_digits = set(concatenated)\n    \n    # Check if all digits 1-9 are present and there are no 0's\n    if actual_digits != expected_digits:\n        return False\n    \n    # Check if each digit appears exactly once\n    digit_count = {}\n    for digit in concatenated:\n        digit_count[digit] = digit_count.get(digit, 0) + 1\n    \n    # All digits should appear exactly once\n    for count in digit_count.values():\n        if count != 1:\n            return False\n    \n    return True\n```",
