      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minimumBeautifulSubstrings(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a binary string s, partitions the string into the minimum number of\n    substrings such that each substring is a power of 5 in binary form and \n    contains no leading zeros.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Precompute binary strings of powers of 5 that could fit into a length-15 string.\n    # 5^0 = 1 (1)\n    # 5^1 = 5 (101)\n    # 5^2 = 25 (11001)\n    # 5^3 = 125 (1111101)\n    # 5^4 = 625 (1001110001)\n    # 5^5 = 3125 (110000110101)\n    # 5^6 = 15625 (11110100001001)\n    # Any higher power of 5 results in a binary representation longer than 15 bits.\n    powers = {\n        \"1\", \n        \"101\", \n        \"11001\", \n        \"1111101\", \n        \"1001110001\", \n        \"110000110101\", \n        \"11110100001001\"\n    }\n    \n    n = len(s)\n    # dp[i] stores the minimum number of beautiful substrings to partition s[0:i].\n    # Initialize with a value larger than any possible partition length (n+1).\n    dp = [float('inf')] * (n + 1)\n    dp[0] = 0\n    \n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        for j in range(i):\n            substring = s[j:i]\n            # Check if the substring is a beautiful string and the previous partition exists.\n            if substring in powers:\n                if dp[j] != float('inf'):\n                    dp[i] = min(dp[i], dp[j] + 1)\n                    \n    return int(dp[n]) if dp[n] != float('inf') else -1\n```",
