      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef numberOfPowerfulInt(start, finish, limit, s):\n    L = len(s)\n    # Compute KMP failure function (longest proper prefix which is also suffix)\n    lps = [0] * L\n    for i in range(1, L):\n        j = lps[i-1]\n        while j > 0 and s[i] != s[j]:\n            j = lps[j-1]\n        if s[i] == s[j]:\n            j += 1\n        lps[i] = j\n\n    # Build transition table for automaton of suffix matching\n    nxt = [[0] * 10 for _ in range(L+1)]\n    for state in range(L+1):\n        for d in range(10):\n            if state < L and int(s[state]) == d:\n                nxt[state][d] = state + 1\n            else:\n                if state == 0:\n                    nxt[state][d] = 0\n                else:\n                    nxt[state][d] = nxt[lps[state-1]][d]\n\n    from functools import lru_cache\n\n    def count_up_to(n):\n        if n < 0:\n            return 0\n        digits = list(map(int, str(n)))\n        length = len(digits)\n\n        @lru_cache(maxsize=None)\n        def dfs(pos, tight, state):\n            if pos == length:\n                return 1 if state == L else 0\n            bound = digits[pos] if tight else 9\n            max_d = min(bound, limit)\n            total = 0\n            for d in range(max_d + 1):\n                new_tight = tight and (d == bound)\n                new_state = nxt[state][d]\n                total += dfs(pos+1, new_tight, new_state)\n            return total\n\n        return dfs(0, True, 0)\n\n    return count_up_to(finish) - count_up_to(start-1)\n```",
