start = min(p, n - k)`\n             - `end = start + k - 1`\n             - `ops += 1`\n             - Skip all positions that are <= `end` (because covered)\n             - `while i < len(positions) and positions[i] <= end: i += 1`\n        - Print `ops`\n\nNote: `n-k` is the last valid start index.\n\nLet's code accordingly.\n\nWe must be careful: `n-k` might be negative? But `k<=n`, so `n-k>=0`.\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Code:\n\n```python\nt = int(input())\nfor _ in range(t):\n    n, k = map(int, input().split())\n    s = input().strip()\n    \n    # Collect positions of black cells\n    blacks = []\n    for i, ch in enumerate(s):\n        if ch == 'B':\n            blacks.append(i)\n    \n    if not blacks:\n        print(0)\n        continue\n    \n    ops = 0\n    i = 0\n    while i < len(blacks):\n        p = blacks[i]\n        start = min(p, n - k)\n        end = start + k - 1\n        ops += 1\n        # Skip all black cells covered by this operation\n        while i < len(blacks) and blacks[i] <= end:\n            i += 1\n    \n    print(ops)\n```\n\nLet's run the sample test cases mentally — already did, it matches.\n\nWe output the code as requested.\n\nNote: The total length of all strings is <= 200,000, so this is efficient.\n\nFinal code below.",
