      "generated_answer": "I need to solve this step by step.\n\n## Problem Understanding\n\n1. We have N boxes numbered 1 to N\n2. Each box i initially contains one ball of color C_i\n3. We process Q queries, each moving all balls from box a to box b\n4. After each move, we print the number of different colors in box b\n5. We need to efficiently track which colors are in each box\n\n## Key Insights\n\n1. We need to maintain the set of colors in each box\n2. When moving from box a to box b, we transfer all colors from a to b\n3. We need to count distinct colors in box b after the transfer\n4. After the move, box a becomes empty\n\n## Algorithm Design\n\n1. Use a list or dictionary to store the set of colors in each box\n2. For each query (a, b):\n   - Move all colors from box a to box b\n   - Count distinct colors in box b\n   - Print the count\n   - Clear box a\n\n## Implementation Strategy\n\n- Use a list of sets where boxes[i] contains the colors in box i+1\n- For each query, update the sets and count distinct colors\n\nLet me trace through Sample Input 1:\n- Initial: boxes = [{1}, {1}, {1}, {2}, {2}, {3}]\n- Query (1,2): Move box 1 to box 2 → box 2 has {1}, box 1 is empty → output 1\n- Query (6,4): Move box 6 to box 4 → box 4 has {2,3}, box 6 is empty → output 2\n- Query (5,1): Move box 5 to box 1 → box 1 has {2}, box 5 is empty → output 1\n- Query (3,6): Move box 3 to box 6 → box 6 has {1}, box 3 is empty → output 1\n- Query (4,6): Move box 4 to box 6 → box 6 has {1,2,3}, box 4 is empty → output 3\n\n## Optimization Note\n\nSince we're only interested in the count of distinct colors, we can use sets which automatically handle uniqueness.\n\n```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read input\n    N, Q = map(int, input().split())\n    colors = list(map(int, input().split()))\n    \n    # Initialize boxes with sets of colors\n    # boxes[i] represents box (i+1)\n    boxes = [set() for _ in range(N)]\n    \n    # Initially, box i contains ball of color C_i\n    for i in range(N):\n        boxes[i].add(colors[i])\n    \n    # Process queries\n    for _ in range(Q):\n        a, b = map(int, input().split())\n        # Convert to 0-indexed\n        a -= 1\n        b -= 1\n        \n        # Move all balls from box a to box b\n        if boxes[a]:  # Only move if box a is not empty\n            boxes[b].update(boxes[a])\n            boxes[a].clear()\n        \n        # Print number of different colors in box b\n        print(len(boxes[b]))\n\nsolve()\n```",
