      "generated_answer": "```python\nfrom typing import List\nimport bisect\n\ndef beautifulIndices(s: str, a: str, b: str, k: int) -> List[int]:\n    n = len(s)\n    len_a, len_b = len(a), len(b)\n    \n    # Collect all starting indices of substring a\n    indices_a = []\n    for i in range(n - len_a + 1):\n        if s[i:i+len_a] == a:\n            indices_a.append(i)\n    \n    # Collect all starting indices of substring b\n    indices_b = []\n    for j in range(n - len_b + 1):\n        if s[j:j+len_b] == b:\n            indices_b.append(j)\n    \n    # If no b occurrences, no index can be beautiful\n    if not indices_b:\n        return []\n    \n    result = []\n    for i in indices_a:\n        # Find the first b index >= i - k\n        pos = bisect.bisect_left(indices_b, i - k)\n        # Check if that position exists and is within i + k\n        if pos < len(indices_b) and indices_b[pos] <= i + k:\n            result.append(i)\n    \n    return result\n```",
