tead, we can:\n# Set all ans[i] = a big number, then set fireworks days to 0, then backward pass.\n\n# Alternatively, simpler:\n# Use a boolean list to check if fireworks occur on day i.\n```\n\nBut the backward recurrence only works if we know the next fireworks day is reachable.\n\nBetter plan:\n\n- Create an array `ans` of size `N+1` (1-indexed).\n- Create a boolean list `is_firework` of size `N+1`, mark fireworks days as True.\n- Set `ans[N] = 0` because last day is fireworks (guaranteed).\n- Then for `i` from `N-1` down to `1`:\n  - If `is_firework[i]`, then `ans[i] = 0`\n  - Else, `ans[i] = ans[i+1] + 1`\n\nThis works perfectly.\n\n---\n\n### **Edge Case**\n\n- If `i = N`, fireworks are launched → 0.\n- Since `A_M = N`, we know `ans[N] = 0`.\n\n---\n\n### **Code Implementation**\n\nLet's code accordingly.\n\nSteps:\n1. Read N, M.\n2. Read list A of M integers.\n3. Create `is_firework` list of size N+1 (index 0 unused or used for 1..N).\n4. Mark `is_firework[a] = True` for each a in A.\n5. Create `ans` array of size N+1.\n6. Set `ans[N] = 0`.\n7. Loop `i` from `N-1` down to `1`:\n   - If `is_firework[i]`: `ans[i] = 0`\n   - Else: `ans[i] = ans[i+1] + 1`\n8. Print `ans[1]`, `ans[2]`, ..., `ans[N]` each on a line.\n\n---\n\n### **Let's Test on Sample 1**\n\nInput:\n```\n3 2\n2 3\n```\n\n- N=3, M=2, A=[2,3]\n- is_firework[2]=True, is_firework[3]=True\n- ans[3] = 0\n- i=2: is_firework[2] → ans[2]=0\n- i=1: not firework → ans[1] = ans[2] + 1 = 1\n\nOutput:\n```\n1\n0\n0\n```\n\nCorrect.\n\n---\n\n### **Final Code**\n\n```python\nimport sys\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    N = int(data[0])\n    M = int(data[1])\n    A = list(map(int, data[2:2+M]))\n    \n    is_firework = [False] * (N + 1)  # 1-indexed up to N\n    for day in A:\n        if day <= N:\n            is_firework[day] = True\n    \n    ans = [0] * (N + 1)  # 1-indexed; we'll use indices 1 to N\n    \n    # Last day is guaranteed to have fireworks\n    ans[N] = 0\n    \n    # Traverse backwards from N-1 down to 1\n    for i in range(N - 1, 0, -1):\n        if is_firework[i]:\n            ans[i] = 0\n        else:\n            ans[i] = ans[i + 1] + 1\n    \n    # Output each answer from day 1 to day N\n    for i in range(1, N + 1):\n        print(ans[i])\n\nmain()\n```",
