      "generated_answer": "I need to solve this step by step.\n\nThis is a shortest path problem where:\n- We start at stage 1\n- We want to reach stage N\n- At each stage i, we have two options:\n  1. Spend A_i seconds to go to stage i+1\n  2. Spend B_i seconds to go to stage X_i\n\nI'll use dynamic programming with Dijkstra's algorithm to find the minimum time to reach each stage.\n\nLet me trace through the first example:\n- N = 5\n- Stage 1: A1=100, B1=200, X1=3 (can go to stage 2 or stage 3)\n- Stage 2: A2=50, B2=10, X2=1 (can go to stage 3 or stage 1)\n- Stage 3: A3=100, B3=200, X3=5 (can go to stage 4 or stage 5)\n- Stage 4: A4=150, B4=1, X4=2 (can go to stage 5 or stage 2)\n\nThe optimal path is:\n- Stage 1 → Stage 2 (cost 100)\n- Stage 2 → Stage 3 (cost 50) \n- Stage 3 → Stage 5 (cost 200)\n- Total: 350\n\nI'll implement Dijkstra's algorithm where each stage is a node, and we have edges representing the two possible actions from each stage.\n\n```python\nimport heapq\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    N = int(input())\n    \n    # Build adjacency list\n    # For each stage, store (next_stage, cost)\n    graph = [[] for _ in range(N + 1)]\n    \n    for i in range(1, N):\n        A, B, X = map(int, input().split())\n        # Option 1: spend A_i to go to stage i+1\n        graph[i].append((i + 1, A))\n        # Option 2: spend B_i to go to stage X_i\n        graph[i].append((X, B))\n    \n    # Dijkstra's algorithm\n    # dist[i] = minimum time to reach stage i\n    dist = [float('inf')] * (N + 1)\n    dist[1] = 0\n    \n    # Priority queue: (time, stage)\n    pq = [(0, 1)]\n    \n    while pq:\n        time, stage = heapq.heappop(pq)\n        \n        # If we've already found a better path to this stage, skip\n        if time > dist[stage]:\n            continue\n            \n        # If we reached stage N, we can return\n        if stage == N:\n            print(time)\n            return\n            \n        # Explore neighbors\n        for next_stage, cost in graph[stage]:\n            new_time = time + cost\n            if new_time < dist[next_stage]:\n                dist[next_stage] = new_time\n                heapq.heappush(pq, (new_time, next_stage))\n    \n    print(dist[N])\n\nsolve()\n```",
