    "prompt": "Generate an executable Python function generated from the given prompt. Return the function body without invoking it at the final solution. Question:\nA powerful array for an integer x is the shortest sorted array of powers of two that sum up to x. For example, the powerful array for 11 is [1, 2, 8].\nThe array big_nums is created by concatenating the powerful arrays for every positive integer i in ascending order: 1, 2, 3, and so forth. Thus, big_nums starts as [1, 2, 1, 2, 4, 1, 4, 2, 4, 1, 2, 4, 8, ...].\nYou are given a 2D integer matrix queries, where for queries[i] = [from_i, to_i, mod_i] you should calculate (big_nums[from_i] * big_nums[from_i + 1] * ... * big_nums[to_i]) % mod_i.\nReturn an integer array answer such that answer[i] is the answer to the i^th query.\n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: queries = [[1,3,7]]\nOutput: [4]\nExplanation:\nThere is one query.\nbig_nums[1..3] = [2,1,2]. The product of them is 4. The remainder of 4 under 7 is 4.\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: queries = [[2,5,3],[7,7,4]]\nOutput: [2,2]\nExplanation:\nThere are two queries.\nFirst query: big_nums[2..5] = [1,2,4,1]. The product of them is 8. The remainder of 8 under 3 is 2.\nSecond query: big_nums[7] = 2. The remainder of 2 under 4 is 2.\n\n \nConstraints:\n\n1 <= queries.length <= 500\nqueries[i].length == 3\n0 <= queries[i][0] <= queries[i][1] <= 10^15\n1 <= queries[i][2] <= 10^5",
    "prediction": "gpt-oss-120b",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "**Python function**\n\n```python\ndef productQueries(queries):\n    \"\"\"\n    queries: List[List[int]] where each sub‑list is [from_i, to_i, mod_i]\n    returns: List[int] – answer for each query\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # ---------- helpers for counting bits and exponent sums ----------\n    def bits_and_exponents_upto(n):\n        \"\"\"\n        Returns a pair (total_set_bits, total_exponent_sum) for the numbers 1..n.\n        total_exponent_sum = Σ (position of each set bit) over the same range.\n        \"\"\"\n        total_bits = 0\n        total_exp = 0\n        i = 0                     # current bit position (0‑based)\n        while (1 << i) <= n:      # only need to go up to the highest set bit of n\n            cycle = 1 << (i + 1)               # length of a full 0/1 cycle for this bit\n            full_cycles = (n + 1) // cycle      # how many complete cycles fit in 0..n\n            total_bits += full_cycles * (1 << i)   # each full cycle contributes 2^i set bits\n            remainder = (n + 1) % cycle\n            extra = max(0, remainder - (1 << i))   # the tail part that may contain extra 1s\n            total_bits += extra\n\n            # each occurrence of this bit contributes its index i to the exponent sum\n            total_exp += i * (full_cycles * (1 << i) + extra)\n\n            i += 1\n        return total_bits, total_exp\n\n    # ---------- prefix exponent sum ----------\n    def prefix_exponent(pos):\n        \"\"\"\n        Returns Σ exponent of the first `pos` elements of the infinite\n        sequence big_nums (0‑based, i.e. positions 0 … pos‑1).\n        If pos == 0 the sum is 0.\n        \"\"\"\n        if pos == 0:\n            return 0\n\n        # find smallest n such that the total number of bits up to n >= pos\n        # first enlarge an upper bound exponentially\n        hi = 1\n        while bits_and_exponents_upto(hi)[0] < pos:\n            hi <<= 1\n\n        lo = 1\n        while lo < hi:\n            mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n            if bits_and_exponents_upto(mid)[0] >= pos:\n                hi = mid\n            else:\n                lo = mid + 1\n        n = lo                      # the integer whose bits contain the (pos‑th) element\n\n        # fully taken numbers are 1 .. n‑1\n        bits_before, exp_before = bits_and_exponents_upto(n - 1)\n\n        # how many bits of the current number n are needed?\n        need = pos - bits_before     # 1 ≤ need ≤ popcount(n)\n\n        # sum of the *lowest* `need` set‑bit positions of n\n        partial = 0\n        tmp = n\n        while need:\n            lsb = tmp & -tmp                 # isolate lowest set bit\n            k = lsb.bit_length() - 1         # its position\n            partial += k\n            tmp ^= lsb                       # remove it\n            need -= 1\n\n        return exp_before + partial\n\n    # ---------- answer each query ----------\n    answers = []\n    for lo, hi, mod in queries:\n        # product of elements = 2^{ exponent_sum }\n        exp_sum = prefix_exponent(hi + 1) - prefix_exponent(lo)\n        answers.append(pow(2, exp_sum, mod))\n    return answers\n```",
