      "generated_answer": "I need to solve this step by step.\n\nThe problem asks for the number of ways to replace each '?' in string S with either '(' or ')' such that the resulting string is a valid parenthesis string.\n\nA valid parenthesis string means:\n- Empty string is valid\n- If A is valid, then (A) is valid\n- If A and B are valid, then AB is valid\n\nThis is equivalent to saying that at every prefix, the number of '(' should be >= number of ')', and at the end, they should be equal.\n\nI'll use dynamic programming:\n- Let dp[i][j] = number of ways to process first i characters such that we have j more '(' than ')' so far\n- j must always be >= 0 (otherwise invalid)\n- At the end, we need j = 0 for a valid string\n\nSteps:\n1. Initialize dp[0][0] = 1\n2. For each character in S:\n   - If it's '(', then dp[i+1][j+1] += dp[i][j]\n   - If it's ')', then dp[i+1][j-1] += dp[i][j] (only if j > 0)\n   - If it's '?', then both options are possible\n3. Answer is dp[n][0] where n is length of S\n\nLet me trace through the first example:\nS = \"(???(?\"\n\n- Position 0: '(' → balance = 1\n- Position 1: '?' → can be '(' (balance=2) or ')' (balance=0)\n- Position 2: '?' → from balance=2: can go to 3 or 1; from balance=0: can go to 1 (can't go to -1)\n- And so on...\n\n```python\ndef solve():\n    MOD = 998244353\n    S = input().strip()\n    n = len(S)\n    \n    # dp[i][j] = number of ways to have balance j after processing first i characters\n    # balance = number of '(' minus number of ')'\n    dp = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n    \n    # Base case: empty prefix has balance 0\n    dp[0][0] = 1\n    \n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(n + 1):\n            if dp[i][j] == 0:\n                continue\n                \n            if S[i] == '(':\n                # Must place '('\n                if j + 1 <= n:\n                    dp[i + 1][j + 1] = (dp[i + 1][j + 1] + dp[i][j]) % MOD\n            elif S[i] == ')':\n                # Must place ')'\n                if j > 0:\n                    dp[i + 1][j - 1] = (dp[i + 1][j - 1] + dp[i][j]) % MOD\n            else:  # S[i] == '?'\n                # Can place '('\n                if j + 1 <= n:\n                    dp[i + 1][j + 1] = (dp[i + 1][j + 1] + dp[i][j]) % MOD\n                # Can place ')'\n                if j > 0:\n                    dp[i + 1][j - 1] = (dp[i + 1][j - 1] + dp[i][j]) % MOD\n    \n    print(dp[n][0])\n\nsolve()\n```",
