] == 'A'\n            aoki_count += 1\n            if aoki_count == target and aoki_reached_target is None:\n                aoki_reached_target = i\n    \n    # Compare when they reached the target\n    if takahashi_reached_target < aoki_reached_target:\n        print('T')\n    else:\n        print('A')\n\nsolve()\n```\n\nWait, I need to reconsider the tie-breaking logic. Let me trace through the examples:\n\nFor sample 2: \"ATTATA\"\n- Both have 3 wins total\n- Takahashi wins: positions 1, 4, 5 (0-indexed: 1, 4, 5)\n- Aoki wins: positions 0, 2, 3 (0-indexed: 0, 2, 3)\n- Takahashi reaches 3 wins at position 5\n- Aoki reaches 3 wins at position 3\n- So Aoki reached 3 wins first, but the expected answer is T.\n\nLet me re-read the problem... \n\nOh wait, I think I misunderstood. Let me check sample 2 again:\n\"ATTATA\" - positions: 0:A, 1:T, 2:T, 3:A, 4:T, 5:A\nWait, that's not right. Let me re-read: \"ATTATA\"\n- Position 0: A (Aoki)\n- Position 1: T (Takahashi) \n- Position 2: T (Takahashi)\n- Position 3: A (Aoki)\n- Position 4: T (Takahashi)\n- Position 5: A (Aoki)\n\nSo Takahashi wins: positions 1, 2, 4 (3 wins)\nAoki wins: positions 0, 3, 5 (3 wins)\n\nTakahashi reaches 3 wins at game 5 (0-indexed position 4)\nAoki reaches 3 wins at game 6 (0-indexed position 5)\n\nSo Takahashi reached 3 wins first (at game 5 vs game 6), so Takahashi wins.\n\nMy logic is correct, but I made an error in reading the string. Let me fix the code:\n\n```python\ndef solve():\n    N = int(input())\n    S = input().strip()\n    \n    # Count total wins\n    takahashi_wins = S.count('T')\n    aoki_wins = S.count('A')\n    \n    # If one has more wins, they win\n    if takahashi_wins > aoki_wins:\n        print('T')\n        return\n    elif aoki_wins > takahashi_wins:\n        print('A')\n        return\n    \n    # If tied, find who reached the final count first\n    target = takahashi_wins  # same as aoki_wins\n    \n    takahashi_count = 0\n    aoki_count = 0\n    \n    # Go through each game\n    for i in range(N):\n        if S[i] == 'T':\n            takahashi_count += 1\n        else:  # S[i] == 'A'\n            aoki_count += 1\n            \n        # Check if either reached the target\n        if takahashi_count == target:\n            print('T')\n            return\n        if aoki_count == target:\n            print('A')\n            return\n\nsolve()\n```",
