      "generated_answer": "I need to solve this step by step.\n\n## Problem Understanding\n\n1. Takahashi wants to buy AtCoder Drink\n2. He has two options:\n   - Pay regular price P yen (no additional purchase needed)\n   - Use discount coupon: pay Q yen for drink + price of one dish (must buy one dish to use coupon)\n3. There are N dishes available, with prices D₁, D₂, ..., Dₙ\n4. Goal: Find the minimum total amount he must pay\n\n## Analysis\n\nThe minimum cost will be the smaller of:\n1. Regular price: P yen (no dish needed)\n2. Discount price + cheapest dish: Q + min(D₁, D₂, ..., Dₙ) yen\n\n## Step-by-step Solution\n\n1. Read the input values: N, P, Q, and the list of dish prices\n2. Find the minimum dish price among all available dishes\n3. Calculate the total cost if using the coupon: Q + min_dish_price\n4. Compare this with the regular price P\n5. Return the minimum of these two options\n\n## Example Walkthrough\n\n**Sample 1:**\n- N=3, P=100, Q=50\n- Dishes: [60, 20, 40]\n- Minimum dish price = 20\n- Coupon option cost: 50 + 20 = 70\n- Regular price: 100\n- Minimum: min(70, 100) = 70 ✓\n\n**Sample 2:**\n- N=3, P=100, Q=50  \n- Dishes: [60000, 20000, 40000]\n- Minimum dish price = 20000\n- Coupon option cost: 50 + 20000 = 20050\n- Regular price: 100\n- Minimum: min(20050, 100) = 100 ✓\n\n## Implementation\n\n```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    # Read first line: N, P, Q\n    line1 = input().split()\n    N = int(line1[0])\n    P = int(line1[1])\n    Q = int(line1[2])\n    \n    # Read second line: dish prices\n    dish_prices = list(map(int, input().split()))\n    \n    # Find minimum dish price\n    min_dish_price = min(dish_prices)\n    \n    # Calculate cost with coupon (discount price + cheapest dish)\n    coupon_cost = Q + min_dish_price\n    \n    # The answer is the minimum between regular price and coupon cost\n    answer = min(P, coupon_cost)\n    \n    print(answer)\n\nsolve()\n```",
