      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef max_good_subarray_sum(nums, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the maximum sum of a subarray such that the absolute difference\n    between its first and last element is exactly k. If no such subarray exists, returns 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    best = {}          # maps value -> minimum prefix sum for that value seen so far\n    prefix = 0         # running sum of elements (prefix[j+1])\n    max_sum = None     # track maximum sum, None means no good subarray yet\n\n    for j, val in enumerate(nums):\n        prefix += val   # now prefix = sum(nums[0..j])\n\n        # Check both possible starting values that satisfy |val - start| == k\n        for target in (val + k, val - k):\n            if target in best:\n                candidate = prefix - best[target]\n                if max_sum is None or candidate > max_sum:\n                    max_sum = candidate\n\n        # Update best for current value as a potential start for future subarrays\n        start_prefix = prefix - val   # prefix sum before index j, i.e., prefix[j]\n        if val not in best or start_prefix < best[val]:\n            best[val] = start_prefix\n\n    return 0 if max_sum is None else max_sum\n```",
