      "generated_answer": "The TCP (Transmission Control Protocol) is primarily responsible for ensuring reliable, ordered, and error-checked delivery of data between applications running on hosts in a network. It handles the transmission of large messages by breaking them into packets, managing their retransmission if lost, and reassembling them at the destination—this works even when the machines are not directly connected. This functionality is best described by option F.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
