    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Let A be a finite set with m elements, and let B be a finite set with n elements. The number of distinct functions mapping A into B is\n\nOptions: \nA. m^n\nB. n!/m!\nC. (n + m)!\nD. m!/(m - n)!\nE. n!/(n - m)!\nF. m!/(n!(m - n)!)\nG. n!\nH. m!/n!\nI. n^m\nJ. n!/(m!(n - m)!)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the number of distinct functions from set A to set B, recall that for each element in A (which has m elements), we must assign exactly one element from B (which has n elements). Since each of the m elements in A has n independent choices in B, the total number of functions is n × n × ... × n (m times), which is n^m.\n\nThus, the correct answer is I.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
