    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the \"target keys\" (finger table start values) for node $N_6$ in a Chord network with identifier space size $M=16$ ($m=\\log_2(16)=4$), we calculate the values for $i=1$ to $4$ using the formula $(n + 2^{i-1}) \\pmod{M}$.\n\n1. For $i=1$: $(6 + 2^0) \\pmod{16} = 7$\n2. For $i=2$: $(6 + 2^1) \\pmod{16} = 8$\n3. For $i=3$: $(6 + 2^2) \\pmod{16} = 10$\n4. For $i=4$: $(6 + 2^3) \\pmod{16} = 14$\n\nThe resulting values are 7, 8, 10, and 14, which corresponds to option C.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
