      "generated_answer": "To interpolate a function $ f(x) $ at $ n+1 $ distinct points, the minimal-degree polynomial that passes through all these points is uniquely determined and has degree at most $ n $. This is because a polynomial of degree $ n $ has $ n+1 $ coefficients, which can be uniquely solved to match the $ n+1 $ function values.\n\nThus, the maximum possible degree of the interpolating polynomial $ p(x) $ is $ n $, though it could be less if the data lies on a lower-degree polynomial.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
