      "generated_answer": "In Thomas Hobbes’ *Leviathan*, he distinguishes between \"vital motion,\" which occurs involuntarily (like heartbeat and breathing), and \"animal motion,\" which is synonymous with \"voluntary motion.\" Animal motion refers to physical actions initiated by the mind, such as walking or speaking, that are preceded by an internal thought or \"fancy.\" Thus, it encompasses all voluntary behavior driven by the imagination.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
