    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "In his essay \"Parenting in the Age of Genetics,\" Peter Singer argues that if a global ban on non-therapeutic genetic enhancement is ineffective, the only alternative to allowing an unregulated, unequal free market would be to ensure everyone has equal access to the technology, potentially through state provision. This is often framed as a \"bolder\" move to avoid the dystopian scenario of a genetic caste system where only the wealthy can afford enhancements.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
