    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: If a test has a standard error of measurement of 15 points, itis correct to conclude that\n\nOptions: \nA. about 85% of the observed scores for the test population lie within 15 points of the mean score\nB. differences of up to 15 points represent the same true score\nC. about 68% of the individuals with a given cure score will have observed scores within 15 points of the true score\nD. about 68% of the observed scores for the test population lie within 15 points of the mean score\nE. about 68% of the observed scores for the test population lie within 30 points of the mean score\nF. about 68% of the observed scores will lie between 15 points below and above the true score\nG. about 32% of the individuals with a given cure score will have observed scores within 15 points of the true score\nH. about 15% of the individuals with a given score will have observed scores within 15 points of the true score\nI. differences of up to 30 points represent the same true score\nJ. about 15% of the scores are in error (i.e., they are not measuring the trait reliably)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
