    "global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2578",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A graduate student’s dissertation chair, Dr. X, turns out to be of little help, and the student ends up obtaining advice and assistance from an associate professor, Dr. Z. Dr. X does review the dissertation when it is completed and she is listed as the dissertation chair. Several months later, the student decides to write an article for a professional journal that is based his dissertation research. In terms of publication credit:\n\nOptions: \nA. Dr. Z should not be listed as an author since she is not the student's official dissertation chair.\nB. Dr. Y and Dr. Z should be listed as co-authors.\nC. Dr. X should be listed as second author since she was the student’s official dissertation chair.\nD. The student should be the sole author as the research is based on his dissertation.\nE. Dr. X should be listed as first author since she was the student’s official dissertation chair.\nF. Dr. Z should be listed as first author if her contribution was substantial.\nG. Dr. X and Dr. Z should be listed as co-authors with no particular order.\nH. Dr. Z should be listed as second author if her contribution warrants it.\nI. Dr. X should be listed as second author and Dr. Z should not be included as an author.\nJ. Dr. Z should be listed as first author, and the student should be listed as second author.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
