  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_psychology_2220",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Dr. Harry Holliday, a clinical psychologist, is planning to take a three-week cruise. In terms of his clinical practice, Dr. Holliday’s best course of action would be to:\n\nOptions: \nA. Leave without informing his clients of his absence.\nB. give his clients a phone number where he can be reached.\nC. Provide his clients with online resources to manage their issues in his absence.\nD. Continue his sessions via phone calls or video conferencing while on vacation.\nE. Inform his clients only a day before his departure about his unavailability.\nF. Cancel all appointments for the duration of his vacation without informing his clients.\nG. discuss his vacation plans with his current clients ahead of time so that they know he’ll be unavailable during that time.\nH. hire a colleague to take over his appointments while he is on vacation.\nI. give his clients the phone number of a colleague who has agreed to accept phone calls in emergencies.\nJ. Arrange for a colleague to provide only emergency sessions, while regular appointments are paused.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Ethical clinical practice requires therapists to plan for interruptions in care to ensure client safety and continuity. Discussing upcoming absences in advance allows clients to process the break and prepare accordingly, which is the standard professional approach. While arranging emergency coverage (Option I) is also a good practice, discussing the absence ahead of time (Option G) is the primary and most essential step in managing the therapeutic relationship during a vacation.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
