0 p.m.\" is **10:00 a.m.**? 10:00 a.m. to 2:30 p.m. = 4.5 hours → 540 / 4.5 = 120 — not listed.\n\nWait — option A is 360 mph → 540 / 360 = 1.5 hours = 1 hr 30 min.\n\nSo if arrival is 2:30 p.m., then departure was 1:00 p.m.\n\nBut \"00 p.m.\" — could that be 1:00 p.m.? Unlikely.\n\n\"00 p.m.\" might be a typo for **1:00 p.m.**? Then 1:00 p.m. to 2:30 p.m. = 1.5 hours.\n\nThen speed = 540 / 1.5 = 360 mph → option A.\n\nThat fits.\n\nAlternatively, 540 miles in 1.5 hours = 360 mph.\n\nSo likely the departure time \"00 p.m.\" is a typo for **1:00 p.m.** (perhaps \"1:00 p.m.\" misread as \"00 p.m.\").\n\nThus, average speed is 360 mph.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
