      "generated_answer": "Negative residual autocorrelation occurs when a positive residual is likely to be followed by a negative one, and vice versa, resulting in an oscillatory or alternating pattern in the residual plot. This behavior corresponds to a Durbin-Watson statistic greater than 2. Therefore, an alternating pattern is the standard indicator of negative autocorrelation.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
