    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: What is the purpose of the National Accounts?\n\nOptions: \nA. National Accounts document the financial transactions of a nation\nB. National Accounts provide a detailed demographic breakdown of a nation's population\nC. National Accounts assess the environmental impact of economic activities\nD. National Accounts monitor the national debt\nE. The National Accounts measure the total value of the output of the economy and show where the output originates and how it is allocated.\nF. National Accounts determine the tax rates for different income brackets\nG. National Accounts regulate international trade agreements\nH. National Accounts track the income of individuals\nI. National Accounts calculate the gross domestic product (GDP) per capita only\nJ. National Accounts compile and analyze consumer spending habits only\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The National Accounts are a system of economic accounts that measure the economic activity of a nation, including production, income, and expenditure. Their primary purpose is to measure the total value of output (such as GDP), show where it comes from (by sector or industry), and how it is used (consumption, investment, etc.). While they do include financial transactions and are used to calculate GDP, the most comprehensive and accurate description is that they measure total output and its origins and allocation.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
