    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Why does Parfit oppose equality?\n\nOptions: \nA. He claims that by giving priority to the needs of the poor, we can increase equality.\nB. He rejects the idea of equality altogether.\nC. He believes that equality is not a realistic goal.\nD. He argues than an unequal society is inevitable.\nE. He suggests that societal structures inherently support inequality.\nF. He asserts that we are each responsible for our poverty.\nG. He posits that striving for equality undermines individual freedoms.\nH. He argues that inequality is necessary for competition and progress.\nI. He contends that inequality is a natural human condition.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Derek Parfit, in his famous essay \"Equality or Priority?\", argues for the \"Priority View\" rather than egalitarianism. He claims that equality is not intrinsically valuable, but rather that we should give priority to the needs of the worst-off, which effectively directs resources toward the poor. Thus, he does not reject fairness but critiques the focus on equality itself.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
