      "generated_answer": "The Uniform Commercial Code (UCC) applies to transactions involving the sale of \"goods,\" which are defined as tangible, movable personal property. While crops and timber are typically considered real property, the UCC explicitly includes contracts for the sale of \"growing crops or other timber to be cut\" under the definition of goods (UCC § 2-107). Other options generally involve real estate (A, F, I), services (B, E, J), or intangible assets/securities (C, H), none of which fall under Article 2 of the UCC.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
