      "generated_answer": "The scenario presented mirrors the \"White Primary\" cases, such as *Smith v. Allwright* and *Terry v. Adams*, in which the Supreme Court held that political parties performing a vital role in the election process are subject to constitutional constraints regarding racial discrimination. Because the Party's exclusion of non-Latinos from the primary effectively denies them the right to participate in the electoral process based on race, it violates the Fifteenth Amendment. Consequently, the federal court would likely grant relief to the plaintiffs.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
