      "generated_answer": "The statute is constitutional because Article I, Section 8, Clause 14 of the U.S. Constitution expressly grants Congress the power to make rules for the government and regulation of the land and naval forces. While the President serves as Commander-in-Chief, this authority does not exempt the military from reasonable legislative regulations concerning its conduct and operations. A notification requirement is a valid exercise of Congressional oversight that does not unduly interfere with the President's tactical command or national security responsibilities.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
