      "generated_answer": "According to Article 2(1)(a) of the Vienna Convention on the Law of Treaties, a treaty is defined as an international agreement concluded between states in written form and governed by international law, regardless of its specific designation or structure. Therefore, the law does not require a treaty to bear a particular title (like \"treaty\" or \"convention\") or adhere to a rigid, predetermined format, provided the document is in writing and intended to be binding. \n\n\\boxed{E}",
