    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Separating the concept of punishment from its justification is a fundamental methodological requirement in the philosophy of law to prevent circular reasoning. By ensuring the definition remains value-neutral, one can analyze the nature of punishment objectively before debating whether it is morally or legally permissible. If the definition included a justification (e.g., \"punishment is the just infliction of pain\"), it would be impossible to critically evaluate whether that infliction is actually justified.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
