      "generated_answer": "Savigny’s *Volksgeist* theory posits that law develops organically from the historical traditions, customs, and culture of a people, specifically rejecting the notion that it is an artificial construct imposed by a sovereign's deliberate legislative will. While options C and F also contradict his views, option A represents the direct antithesis to his core thesis, which he famously argued against in his debate over the codification of German law. Therefore, the assertion that law is merely the result of a sovereign's intentional command is the most fundamental contradiction to the Historical School's belief in organic legal evolution.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
