      "generated_answer": "The deed created a fee simple subject to a condition subsequent with a right of entry retained by the grantor, which is a transferable interest that passed to the daughters upon the grantor's death. Because the original deed containing the restriction was properly recorded, the developer had constructive notice of the condition and is bound by it, regardless of whether the restriction appeared in the subsequent deed from the wife. Therefore, the daughters can enforce their right of entry or seek an injunction to prevent the violation of the condition.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
