    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Lev Vygotsky's theory emphasizes the Zone of Proximal Development (ZPD), which refers to the difference between what a learner can do without help and what they can achieve with guidance. The process through which a child's unaided learning ability develops is known as internalization—the transformation of social interactions and guided learning into independent cognitive functioning. This process allows the child to gradually perform tasks independently that they initially needed help with.\n\n\\boxed{internalization}",
      "success": true,
