estricted mass tourism was leading to damaging long-term consequences also began to grow. By the late 1990s, a new emphasis on quality and, especially in the Balearics, on safeguarding the environment had finally taken root—too late for many environmentalists, but hopefully still in time to preserve much of the natural beauty and unique character of the Las Islas Baleares. \nQuestion: Why was there not very high tourism in Spain during Franco's regime and what happened that allow tourism to increase\n\nProvided Answer: \n\n Is the provided answer correct? Provide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct choice. ",
