    "global index": "AsDiv_1425",
    "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem step by step. \n\nContext: A boat goes 30 km upstream and 44 km downstream in 10 hours. In 13 hours, it can go 40 km upstream and 55 km downstream.\n\nQuestion: Determine the speed of the stream and that of boat in still water.\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let the speed of the boat in still water be $ b $ km/h and the speed of the stream be $ s $ km/h. Then, the speed upstream is $ b - s $ and downstream is $ b + s $. Using the formula $ \\text{time} = \\frac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{speed}} $, we form two equations from the given scenarios:\n\n$$\n\\frac{30}{b - s} + \\frac{44}{b + s} = 10 \\quad \\text{(1)}\n$$\n$$\n\\frac{40}{b - s} + \\frac{55}{b + s} = 13 \\quad \\text{(2)}\n$$\n\nLet $ x = \\frac{1}{b - s} $ and $ y = \\frac{1}{b + s} $. Then the equations become:\n$$\n30x + 44y = 10 \\quad \\text{(1a)}\n$$\n$$\n40x + 55y = 13 \\quad \\text{(2a)}\n$$\n\nMultiply (1a) by 4 and (2a) by 3:\n$$\n120x + 176y = 40\n$$\n$$\n120x + 165y = 39\n$$\n\nSubtracting: $ 11y = 1 \\Rightarrow y = \\frac{1}{11} $. Substitute into (1a):\n$$\n30x + 44 \\cdot \\frac{1}{11} = 10 \\Rightarrow 30x + 4 = 10 \\Rightarrow 30x = 6 \\Rightarrow x = \\frac{1}{5}\n$$\n\nNow, $ x = \\frac{1}{b - s} = \\frac{1}{5} \\Rightarrow b - s = 5 $, and $ y = \\frac{1}{b + s} = \\frac{1}{11} \\Rightarrow b + s = 11 $. Adding: $ 2b = 16 \\Rightarrow b = 8 $, so $ s = 3 $.\n\n\\boxed{{8, 3}}",
      "success": true,
